      {
        "id": "f1-your-places",
        "name": "Your places (and which one Today uses)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 26,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Your places (and which one Today uses) · f1-your-places\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Saved places\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: (1) the current \"Saved places\" screen on iOS and on Android; (2) a web capture of the current web saved-places page (today it is a bare 760px page with no sidebar and no tab bar); (3) the web Place tab shell at 1440 (left sidebar) and 390 (four-tab bar), which this list moves into; (4) Today's location row showing the \"Saved place · Only you\" chip; (5) the Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915 · web 1440x900 with the left sidebar, Place selected · web 390x844 with the four-tab bar, Place selected. On every web frame, draw the list inside the normal Place shell at /app/place/saved.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab. Entry points: (1) the Place tab itself for anyone with no claimed home: this list is the tab's first screen; (2) tapping the \"Saved place · Only you\" chip in Today's location row; (3) the place file's Address row; (4) \"See your places\" on the save confirmation; (5) on iOS, the existing saved-places route from the feed context bar; (6) Today's one-time notice after a claim (owned by the Today tab), which opens this list with the arrival line described below; (7) proposed: the Notifications settings caption that names the place briefings follow; (8) the Add a place sheet, when opened from here, returns here after saving. When the person arrives from the Today chip, scroll the row Today uses into view once, fade its highlight, and move accessibility focus to that row. Where actions lead: Open goes to that place's place file. Claim this address opens the existing claim flow, which ends on the claim receipt. + Add a place opens the Add a place sheet. After Remove, Today never shows that address again, even if Today is already open: a removed address still showing on Today reads as a privacy failure on an \"Only you\" surface.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Jordan Lee, 36, moved from Portland to PLACE B, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, on Fri 9 Oct and saved it Sat 10 Oct. On Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM Today shows Birchfield. He taps the chip to check that Today isn't using Mom's house, which he saved in September while planning the move.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: See every place you saved, see which one Today uses and why, and switch, claim or remove it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the top row, which carries the only \"Used for Today\" badge, then on the sentence directly under it that says why, then on the other rows, which carry no badge. The one primary action is \"+ Add a place\" at the foot of the list. Row actions live in each row's menu.\n\nCONTENT (Jordan, except where marked):\nTitle \"Your places\". Directly under the title, the ScopeChip saved-place variant \"Saved place · Only you\". It replaces the retired line \"Only you can see these.\"\nEach row: label · city, state and ZIP · saved date. The row Today uses comes first, then the rest, newest first:\n- 1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Camas, WA 98607 · Saved Sat 10 Oct · badge \"Used for Today\". Under it: \"Today uses the address you saved most recently.\"\n- Mom's house · Camas, WA 98607 · Saved Fri 4 Sep\n- The Blairmont rental · Vancouver, WA 98683 · Saved Fri 28 Aug\n- Sister's apartment · Portland, OR 97214 · Saved Sun 19 Jul\n- Worst case: Grandma and Grandpa's lake house on Lacamas Shores Drive · Camas, WA 98607 · Saved Wed 1 Jul\nFoot row: \"+ Add a place\".\nSaved-row menu, in this order: Open · Use for Today · Claim this address · Remove. The badged row never offers Use for Today.\nChosen place: after Use for Today on Mom's house, the badge moves to that row, the row moves to the top, and the sentence reads \"Today uses this place because you chose it.\" The status line reads \"Today now uses Mom's house.\"\nToday using a location not in the list: no row is badged. A single line sits above the list: \"Today is using a location you looked at recently, not one of these. Choose Use for Today on a place to switch.\" (For a pin set elsewhere: \"Today is using a location you pinned, not one of these. Choose Use for Today on a place to switch.\") Every saved row, including Birchfield, offers Use for Today.\nMaya (HOME A): the list splits into two groups with plain labels. Group \"Your home\": 2418 NE Larkspur Loop · Vancouver, WA 98684 · Claimed Tue 1 Sep, with the home glyph, the ScopeChip \"Your household\" and the caption \"Today uses your home\". Group \"Saved places\", with the \"Saved place · Only you\" chip in its group header: Mom's house · Camas, WA 98607 · Saved Fri 4 Sep, then Sam's old apartment · Vancouver, WA 98661 · Saved Sat 15 Aug.\nMaya just claimed (frame 9): the home row reads \"Claimed Mon 19 Oct\"; she had saved 2418 NE Larkspur Loop before, and that saved row is gone.\nMaya arriving from Today's notice (frame 10): the LandingBannerSlot line \"Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. Mom's house is still saved.\" with a trailing \"Close\", above the groups; home row \"Claimed Mon 19 Oct\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: Top bar. No home (Jordan): tab-root title \"Your places\" with no back control (iOS large title; Android top app bar without a navigation icon; web page title in the Place shell). Home users (Maya): a pushed screen with a back control labelled \"Place\" (iOS back chevron; Android navigation arrow; web breadcrumb \"Place / Your places\").\nList. A plain vertical list. In Jordan's frames exactly one row carries the StatusChip \"Used for Today\" variant: surface.sunken fill, text.strong label, a leading 12pt sun-outline glyph in text.strong (not a check, not a circle), not tappable. Every other saved row carries nothing: one badge slot, one menu button, no chips, no radio column. Only the home row carries a chip (ScopeChip \"Your household\"). Put the precedence sentence (bodySmall, text.secondary) directly under the badged row, never in the page header. Show \"Today uses the address you saved most recently.\" only when Today's source is a saved place and nothing is chosen; show \"because you chose it\" only when the person picked it; show the above-list line only when Today uses a location that is not a row.\nWith a home: split into \"Your home\" and \"Saved places\" groups; the saved-place chip moves into the Saved places group header. The home row carries no StatusChip; its caption \"Today uses your home\" is the Today marker and its reason, and no saved row is badged. If Today uses a viewed or pinned location for a home user, the home row drops its caption and the above-list line appears instead. Draw the home row as a home, not a disabled saved place: home glyph (home pillar token, icon only), \"Your household\" chip, the caption. The home row's menu has only Open, which goes to the place file: no Use for Today, Claim or Remove. Leaving a home stays in home settings behind DestructiveConfirm and is not drawn here.\nThis list is the answer to \"where does Today get this address\"; there is no second sheet. Row menu form: iOS pull-down menu from the More button; Android Material 3 dropdown menu; web-1440 popover; web-390 bottom sheet with Close. Menus never stack on another sheet. When the service cannot say which place Today uses, draw no badge and show an InlineErrorRow in the sentence slot.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Tapping a row opens it. Tapping the menu button (44pt / 48dp / 44px) opens the menu. Use for Today: the menu closes, the badge stays where it is until the save succeeds, and the sentence slot shows \"Switching Today to Mom's house…\" only if the save takes 1s or longer; on success the badge and row move; on failure the InlineErrorRow appears. Remove collapses the row in place to an InlineUndo (height change 300ms or less), and the badge cross-fades to the next row in the same frame. Undo stays until the person leaves the screen; no timer and no confirm dialog. This replaces Android's 4-second snackbar. If the removal fails on the server, the row comes back in place, the badge returns to its original row, and an InlineErrorRow sits under that row. Tapping the header ScopeChip expands one explanation in place: \"Saved places are only for you. To share one with the people you live with, claim it.\" plus a text button \"Claim this address\" for the place Today uses. Every LandingBannerSlot line on this screen has a trailing 44pt action: the sync line uses \"Review\"; the account-switch and claim-notice arrival lines use \"Close\". One banner at a time. A successful Use for Today gives one light haptic tick; nothing else has a haptic. With Reduce Motion on, every change is a cross-fade. No swipe-only actions: every row action is also a menu item.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ScopeChip (saved-place variant, expandable, under the title or in the Saved places group header; \"Your household\" variant on the home row) · StatusChip (new \"Used for Today\" variant, sun-outline glyph, saved rows only) · InlineUndo (removed-row variant, consequence in the same line) · WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton with the badge slot reserved) · OfflineNotice with FreshnessLine (offline variant) · InlineErrorRow (load failed; Use for Today failed; remove failed) · LandingBannerSlot (sync merge V6 with Review; new account-switched and claim-notice arrival variants with Close; one at a time).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: title, scope chip (or group label and chip), the Today row, the precedence sentence, other rows, + Add a place. Each row is one element, for example: \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, Washington 98607. Saved Saturday 10 October. Used for Today.\" Its custom actions are Open, Claim this address and Remove; the visible menu button reads \"More for 1107 NE Birchfield Ct\". Arriving from the Today chip moves accessibility focus to the row Today uses; arriving from Today's claim notice moves focus to the arrival line. The badge is a word, never only a colour; the sun-outline and home glyphs are decorative, and the home row's caption carries its meaning. A disabled Use for Today stays focusable and gives its reason. Removed rows, the remove-failed row, the switching line, the sync line and arrival lines are role=status. Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px. At AX5 the label, city and saved date stack, the badge moves under the label, and labels wrap and never ellipsise.\n\nCOPY: \"Your places\" · \"Place\" (back label) · \"Saved place · Only you\" · \"Your household\" · \"Your home\" · \"Saved places\" · \"Used for Today\" · \"Today uses the address you saved most recently.\" · \"Today uses this place because you chose it.\" · \"Today is using a location you looked at recently, not one of these. Choose Use for Today on a place to switch.\" · \"Today is using a location you pinned, not one of these. Choose Use for Today on a place to switch.\" · \"Today uses your home\" · \"Your claimed home comes first.\" (reason under a disabled Use for Today) · \"Claimed Tue 1 Sep\" · \"Claimed Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Joined Tue 1 Sep\" · \"Saved Sat 10 Oct\" · \"Open\" · \"Use for Today\" · \"Claim this address\" · \"Remove\" · \"More for 1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" · \"+ Add a place\" · \"Switching Today to Mom's house…\" · \"Removed \\\"The Blairmont rental\\\" · Undo\" · \"Removed \\\"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\\\" · Today now uses Mom's house · Undo\" · \"Removed \\\"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\\\" · Today will ask for a place · Undo\" · \"We couldn't remove \\\"The Blairmont rental\\\" · Retry\" · \"We couldn't remove \\\"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\\\" · Retry\" · \"Today now uses Mom's house.\" · \"Saved places are only for you. To share one with the people you live with, claim it.\" · Empty: \"No places yet\" / \"Save an address and Today will show its weather, air, alerts and dates.\" / \"+ Add a place\" · \"You switched accounts. These are the places saved to this account.\" · \"Synced 3 items from your other device · Review\" · \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" · \"You're offline. You can open your places. Changes need a connection.\" · \"We couldn't load your places · Retry\" · \"We couldn't change the place Today uses · Retry\" · \"Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. Mom's house is still saved.\" · Today's own line after the last removal (owned by the Today tab): \"Today starts with a place\" · \"Close\".\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest label wraps to three lines. With 12 places the list scrolls with no pagination, and the Today row stays first. Zero places shows the empty state. On a slow network, skeletons appear only after 1s, with the badge slot reserved. If Jordan removes his last place, the undo row says Today will ask for a place. A household member such as Sam Ortega sees 2418 NE Larkspur Loop under \"Your home\" with \"Your household\" and \"Joined Tue 1 Sep\" in place of \"Claimed\". A saved place outside Clark County looks like any other row, with no warning. Claiming a different address first shows a one-time notice on Today; tapping it lands here with the arrival line. Claiming the saved address shows it once, as a home, and the old saved row is gone. If Today uses a viewed or pinned location for Maya, the home row drops its caption and the above-list other-location line appears. Offline, Open works from cache; Use for Today, Claim and Remove are disabled with the reason.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a chip or status on every row, draw one StatusChip on one saved row — because one mark reads instantly.\n- Instead of a check glyph or a toggled-looking selected chip for \"Used for Today\", draw the neutral StatusChip with a sun-outline glyph — because it is a status, not a control, and the check belongs to Paid and selected choices.\n- Instead of a radio group or settings picker, draw a list with a row menu — because this is a list of places, not a preference.\n- Instead of a greyed-out saved row for a claimed home, draw a home row in its own \"Your home\" group with Open as its only action — because it is a fact, and leaving a home belongs in home settings.\n- Instead of one \"Only you\" chip over a list that holds a home, split the groups and chip each — because scope must be true for every row.\n- Instead of a separate \"Where Today gets this\" sheet, put the reason beside the badged row or on the home row, or above the list when Today uses something else — because this list already answers that.\n- Instead of a \"Remove this place?\" dialog or a timed snackbar, collapse the row to Removed · Undo — because lasting undo is safer.\n- Instead of \"home\" or \"household\" on saved rows, use \"Saved place\" — because a saved place is shared with nobody.\n\nDONE WHEN: A web person who saved a place reaches this list from the Place tab and from the Today chip. Anyone can say which place Today uses and why within five seconds, including when it is not a row and when they have a home. No caption on screen contradicts another. Removing the Today place moves the badge in the same frame, a removed place never lingers on Today, and a failed removal visibly puts it back. A claimed address appears once, as a home, with no Remove. Every frame reads correctly in greyscale and at AX5.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f1-your-places · ios · 01-multi-place · light — Jordan's five rows, Birchfield with the StatusChip and its sentence, header chip, tab-root large title with no back control, + Add a place.\n2. f1-your-places · web-1440 · 01-multi-place · light — same rows in the Place shell; popover open on Mom's house.\n3. f1-your-places · android · 01-multi-place · light — same rows, Material 3 list, top app bar with no navigation icon.\n4. f1-your-places · web-390 · 01-multi-place · light — four-tab bar; the lake-house label wraps to three lines; bottom-sheet menu with Close open on it.\n5. f1-your-places · ios · 02-single-place-menu · light — Birchfield only; pull-down menu shows Open, Claim this address, Remove.\n6. f1-your-places · android · 03-chip-expanded · light — single place; header chip expanded with explanation and Claim this address.\n7. f1-your-places · ios · 04-home-outranks · light — Maya, pushed screen with back chevron \"Place\": \"Your home\" (caption \"Today uses your home\", no StatusChip) and \"Saved places\" groups; the home row's menu open showing only Open.\n8. f1-your-places · android · 19-home-user-saved-row-menu · light — Maya, navigation arrow: dropdown on Mom's house with Use for Today disabled and \"Your claimed home comes first.\"\n9. f1-your-places · android · 05-just-claimed · light — Maya, \"Claimed Mon 19 Oct\", no duplicate saved row.\n10. f1-your-places · web-390 · 20-claim-notice-arrival · light — Maya arriving from Today's notice; arrival line with Close above the groups; breadcrumb \"Place / Your places\".\n11. f1-your-places · android · 17-today-uses-other-location · light — Jordan's rows, no badge, the above-list line, Use for Today available on Birchfield's menu.\n12. f1-your-places · ios · 06-removed-undo · light — Birchfield undo line with its consequence; Mom's house now badged.\n13. f1-your-places · ios · 18-remove-failed · light — Birchfield restored with its badge; InlineErrorRow under it.\n14. f1-your-places · web-390 · 07-chosen-for-today · light — Mom's house badged with \"because you chose it\" and the status line.\n15. f1-your-places · android · 08-last-place-removed · light — undo line \"Today will ask for a place\" above the empty state.\n16. f1-your-places · ios · 09-empty · light — No places yet, + Add a place.\n17. f1-your-places · android · 10-loading · light — row skeletons with badge slots reserved.\n18. f1-your-places · ios · 11-offline · light — cached rows, disabled actions with the reason.\n19. f1-your-places · web-1440 · 12-error · light — InlineErrorRow with Retry, shell intact.\n20. f1-your-places · web-1440 · 13-account-switched · light — account-switch line with Close and that account's rows.\n21. f1-your-places · android · 14-synced · light — \"Synced 3 items from your other device · Review\" in the banner slot.\n22. f1-your-places · ios · 15-ax5 · light — frame 1 content at AX5.\n23. f1-your-places · ios · 16-greyscale · light — frame 7 in greyscale.\n24. f1-your-places · ios · 01-multi-place · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n25. f1-your-places · ios · 04-home-outranks · dark — same groups, back chevron and home-row menu as frame 7.\n26. f1-your-places · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — Notes: assumptions; every invented string (Sister's apartment, The Blairmont rental, Mom's house, the lake-house label, Sam's old apartment, all saved/claimed/joined dates, the group labels, the back label, the chosen, switching, other-location and pinned lines, the undo and remove-failed lines, the chip explanation, \"Your claimed home comes first.\", \"Today uses your home\"); the new StatusChip \"Used for Today\" variant with its sun-outline glyph in text.strong (chosen so it does not borrow Paid's check); the home row carrying only the ScopeChip and no StatusChip; the home-row menu holding only Open; new LandingBannerSlot variants: account-switched and claim-notice arrival, each with Close; V6 keeps the contract's \"Synced\" wording pending founder decision 5.2; \"A home you've claimed always wins\" (inventory) is replaced by the home-row caption \"Today uses your home\" and the disabled reason \"Your claimed home comes first.\"; omitted states (the switching-in-progress line, drawn only as copy; the pinned-location variant of frame 11; the home user whose Today runs on a viewed or pinned location, drawn only as copy); the fixture note that Jordan's four older saved places predate his Sat 10 Oct save, while the add-place, save and email projects draw that save differently, for the founder to reconcile; the merge note that Your places is the first Place screen when there is no claimed home (the place file prompt also calls itself the Place tab index); and the resolver open question: \"Today's location is resolved in this order: a pinned location, a recently viewed location, then a home. 'Use for Today' writes the pin, and a recent viewing location also outranks a home. For 'Today uses your home' to be true, the server must rank the home above both for home users (refusing or clearing the pin), or the caption must change.\"\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue. Turn 5: 25-26.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Home-row caption changed from 'Today always uses your home' to 'Today uses your home'; added rule that a home user whose Today runs on a viewed or pinned location loses the caption and gets the above-list line (review major + minor; doc §3 resolver order).",
          "Notes open question extended to cover the recently viewed location as well as the pin (review major).",
          "Removal sentence replaced: a removed address never shows on Today again, even if open, with the privacy reason restored from the inventory uxNote (review minor).",
          "Stated that the home row carries no StatusChip and its caption is the Today marker; reworded 'no chips' to 'every other saved row ... Only the home row carries a chip' (review minors; contract StatusChip 'No two chips on one row').",
          "Deep-link arrival from the Today chip now moves accessibility focus to the row; claim-notice arrival moves focus to the arrival line (review minors; brief §5).",
          "Notes record that the inventory string 'A home you've claimed always wins' is replaced (review minor).",
          "LandingBannerSlot lines each get a trailing 44pt action: sync uses the board's V6 'Synced 3 items from your other device · Review'; account-switched and claim-notice use Close; new variants and 'Synced' wording recorded on Notes (review minor).",
          "Added top-bar rule: tab root with no back control for no-home users; pushed screen with back 'Place' / breadcrumb for home users; artboard lines updated (review minor).",
          "'Used for Today' StatusChip glyph changed from primary.700 check to a sun-outline in text.strong; recorded on Notes; INSTEAD OF updated (review minor).",
          "Replaced angle-bracket template strings with concrete strings (Claimed Tue 1 Sep, Joined Tue 1 Sep, Saved Sat 10 Oct, More for 1107 NE Birchfield Ct) (review minor).",
          "Entry point (4) renamed to 'See your places' to match the save confirmation rename; added entry (8) for the Add a place sheet returning here; frame 10 reference corrected (cross-prompt consistency).",
          "Fixture reconcile note broadened to cover the add-place, save and email projects."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f1-add-place-sheet",
        "name": "Add a place (signed-in address search + save)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 23,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Add a place · f1-add-place-sheet\n\nTYPE: NEW. It is a sheet; nothing like it exists for a signed-in person on web or Android.\n\nATTACH: (1) Today's no-place card and (2) the Your places list and its empty state, as backdrops; (3) Today's location row with the \"Saved place · Only you\" chip; (4) the existing iOS save-place sheet, as a reference for sheet chrome only; (5) the Foundations board; (6) Today in its warming state for a saved place (iOS and web-1440), as the backdrop for frames 12 and 13; (7) Maya's Your places on Android from the f1-your-places project, if drawn, as the backdrop for frame 17.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852: the sheet opens at the large detent while the field has focus, with a grabber and a visible Close. Android 412x915: a full-height Material 3 modal bottom sheet that resizes above the keyboard, with a visible Close. Web 1440x900: a centred 560-wide modal with Close. Web 390x844: a bottom sheet with Close. On iOS and Android, Save and the \"Only you will see this.\" caption stay pinned above the keyboard. Host behind the sheet: on web-1440 the sidebar stays visible and dimmed behind the modal; on web-390 the host stays dimmed above the sheet; on iOS and Android only the top of the dimmed host shows above the sheet.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The sheet opens over Today and over the Place tab. Entry points: (1) Today's no-place card, whose button is now \"Add a place\" (it was \"Preview an address\"); (2) \"+ Add a place\" on Your places, in the empty state and at the list foot; (3) a widget tap when there is no place (the widget reads \"Save an address to see today here\"), which opens Today with this sheet on top; (4) the widget how-to's \"Save an address first\" button, which lands in the same place as (3); (5) the place file's Address row when it is empty; (6) proposed: \"Save this address\" on the signed-in compare arrival header. \"Preview an address\" stays only on buttons that really go to the /start preview. The sheet receives nothing, except from the compare arrival header, where it opens in the selected state (03) with the address the person just typed already confirmed.\nWhere it leads: on success the sheet returns to where it opened. From Today, the widget, the place file's empty Address row or the compare header, it dismisses onto Today: Today's location row reads \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\" (when Today switched), Today opens in its warming state, and a one-line role=status row sits directly under the location row until the person leaves Today (not a toast). From Your places, it dismisses onto Your places: the new row appears at the top (with the \"Used for Today\" StatusChip if Today switched), and a role=status line under the title reads \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" with a text button \"See Today\". For a home user, a chosen-place user or a viewed/pinned-location user, that line uses the matching \"Today still uses…\" string below, and they stay on Your places.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Jordan Lee, 36, moved from Portland to PLACE B on Fri 9 Oct. On Sat 10 Oct at 6:10 PM, the day after the move, he opens Your places on his iPhone, taps \"+ Add a place\" and types his new address from memory, misspelled: \"1107 NE Birchfeild\". He already has older saved places, including Mom's house. These frames are dated Sat 10 Oct, the fixture save day, not TODAY. Frame 5 shows the unnamed signed-in first-place case over Today's no-place card; the sheet shows no name.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Type one address, save it privately, and see truthfully which place Today now runs on.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the focused \"Street address\" field (caret in it, keyboard up on iOS and Android), then on the suggestion list beneath, then on the Save button with \"Only you will see this.\" under it. Save is the single primary action.\n\nCONTENT:\nTitle \"Add a place\". Field label \"Street address\". Caption under the field: \"We use the address you type — no location access.\"\nTyped value: \"1107 NE Birchfeild\". Five plain-text suggestions, ranked by distance from Camas and Vancouver, forgiving the typo:\n- 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\n- 1107 NE Birch St, Camas, WA 98607\n- 1170 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\n- 1107 NW Birch Ave, Vancouver, WA 98685\n- 1107 SE Birchwood Dr, Portland, OR 97202\nSelected: the address appears as one confirmed line (AddressChip, selected) above the button. Button \"Save\". Directly under the button: \"Only you will see this.\" When the person already has a saved place and nothing else is in charge of Today, add a caption under Save: \"Today will switch to this address. You can change it in Your places.\" (not shown on the first-place frame).\nNot found: \"We couldn't find that address.\" plus the text button \"Can't find it? Enter it line by line\". It opens five fields in the same sheet: \"Street address\" (keeps the typed text), \"Apt, suite or unit\" (optional), \"City\", \"State\" (a picker, default \"WA\") and \"ZIP code\".\nLookup service down: the manual fields open with \"Address search isn't working right now. Enter it line by line instead.\"\nOutside Clark County: \"1402 NE 33rd Ave, Portland, OR 97232\". Save stays enabled, and one line appears under the address: \"Flood, wildfire, air and radon readings work here. Pickup days and local deadlines are on file only in Clark County, WA for now.\"\nDuplicate: typing \"408 NE Juniper St\" matches Mom's house. That suggestion row reads \"Already saved as Mom's house · Fri 4 Sep\". Selecting it shows the AddressChip duplicate variant with the dated message \"You already saved this as “Mom’s house” on Fri 4 Sep.\" The primary becomes \"Use for Today\", with a text button \"Open it\".\nSaved status (Today's status row, or the line on Your places): \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\"\nChosen-place variant (if Jordan had picked Mom's house with Use for Today): \"Saved privately. Today still uses Mom's house, the place you chose.\"\nViewed-location variant (Today runs on a location he looked at recently that is not a saved row): \"Saved privately. Today still uses the location you looked at recently.\" Pinned twin: \"Saved privately. Today still uses the location you pinned.\"\nClaimed-home variant (Maya, HOME A): \"Saved privately. Today still uses your home.\"\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: A deliberately compact sheet: one field, a plain list, one button and one scope sentence. No map, pin, thumbnail, reading, grade, \"what you'll get\" list, progress dots or second page, because the reading appears on Today a second later. Suggestion rows are text only (48pt / 48dp / 44px), with the untyped part at medium weight in the same size as the row text. The not-found message, manual fields, outside-area line and duplicate chip replace the suggestion list in place; the sheet never opens a second page, and it keeps its height when a state replaces the list so nothing resizes under the thumb. In the duplicate state, the AddressChip duplicate variant shows its message only; its inline \"Use for Today\" action is hidden because the primary button carries it. At AX5 the sheet scrolls. On Today after saving, the status row is one line directly under the location row (bodySmall, text.primary). On Your places after saving, the status line sits under the title and above the list.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Suggestions update as the person types. No indicator for lookups under 1s; after that, \"Looking up addresses…\" in the list slot. Tapping a suggestion selects it and enables Save. Save shows its loading state and locks the field. On success the sheet dismisses with the platform transition onto the screen it opened from, and iOS and Android give one light haptic tick. \"See Today\" on the Your places status line opens Today. Close, Android Back and web Escape discard the sheet and return focus to the button that opened it. After a successful save, focus goes to the status row or line. With Reduce Motion on, list changes and dismissal are cross-fades.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: AddressChip (selected state; duplicate variant with a dated message and its inline action hidden) · ScopeChip (sentence form \"Only you will see this.\"; the saved-place chip on Today) · StatusChip (\"Used for Today\" on the new row on Your places, as drawn in that project) · OfflineNotice (form-offline variant) · InlineErrorRow (save-failed variant, value kept).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Title \"Add a place\" is unique, and focus is trapped in the sheet. The field uses street-address autofill; ZIP code uses a number keyboard; State is a labelled picker. \"5 addresses found\" and each error are announced politely and tied to the field. Each suggestion row is one element that reads the full address. Save's disabled state explains itself: \"Pick an address first\". Focus stays visible above the keyboard. The status row on Today and the status line on Your places are role=status. At AX5, the manual fields are one column and addresses wrap. Nothing depends on colour.\n\nCOPY: \"Add a place\" · \"Close\" · \"Street address\" · \"We use the address you type — no location access.\" · \"Looking up addresses…\" · \"5 addresses found\" (spoken) · \"Save\" · \"Only you will see this.\" · \"Today will switch to this address. You can change it in Your places.\" · \"Pick an address first\" · \"We couldn't find that address.\" · \"Can't find it? Enter it line by line\" · \"Apt, suite or unit\" · \"City\" · \"State\" · \"ZIP code\" · \"Address search isn't working right now. Enter it line by line instead.\" · \"Flood, wildfire, air and radon readings work here. Pickup days and local deadlines are on file only in Clark County, WA for now.\" · \"Already saved as Mom's house · Fri 4 Sep\" · \"You already saved this as “Mom’s house” on Fri 4 Sep.\" · \"Use for Today\" · \"Open it\" · \"See Today\" · \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" · \"Saved privately. Today still uses Mom's house, the place you chose.\" · \"Saved privately. Today still uses the location you looked at recently.\" · \"Saved privately. Today still uses the location you pinned.\" · \"Saved privately. Today still uses your home.\" · \"We saved it, but couldn't place it on a map yet. Today will show it once we can.\" · \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\" · \"Saving needs a connection.\" · \"We couldn't save that place. Your address is still here. Try again.\" · \"Try again\"\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest address, \"12808 NE Lacamas Shores Rd, Unit 204, Camas, WA 98607\", wraps to two lines in the list and the chip; entered by hand, the unit goes in \"Apt, suite or unit\". At most five suggestions. Zero suggestions shows the not-found frame. A manual address that can't be placed on a map still saves, and the status reads \"We saved it, but couldn't place it on a map yet. Today will show it once we can.\" A slow save keeps the button loading, never a full-sheet spinner. Offline, the field and Save are disabled with reasons, and the typed text stays. If the duplicate is already the Today place, the primary becomes \"See Today\". For Maya or any claimed-home user, the save does not change Today, the \"Today will switch\" caption is not shown, and a duplicate's primary becomes \"Open it\" (Use for Today is not offered to home users). A person who chose a place with Use for Today, or whose Today runs on a recently viewed or pinned location, gets the matching \"Today still uses…\" line and no \"Today will switch\" caption.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a map, pin, preview card or reading, draw one field and a plain list — because this sheet only saves, and Today shows the reading.\n- Instead of \"Preview an address\" on buttons that open this sheet, write \"Add a place\" — because a label must predict where it goes.\n- Instead of a link to /start, keep the person signed in, in this sheet — because /start is the signed-out funnel.\n- Instead of always jumping to Today after saving, return to the screen the sheet opened from — because someone adding from Your places expects to see the new row.\n- Instead of refusing an address outside Clark County, save it and name the layers that work there — because the preview works nationwide, and a false \"not served\" is the top complaint about address apps.\n- Instead of a dead-end \"couldn't find\" message, offer line-by-line fields, with a unit line, in the same sheet — because people fall back to typing when autocomplete fails.\n- Instead of asking someone to retype a saved address or one they just typed on the compare header, show it selected or as an \"Already saved\" row — because we already hold it.\n- Instead of silently switching Today, or claiming it switched when a chosen place, a home, or a viewed or pinned location stays in charge, name what Today uses — because nobody should be surprised by what Today shows.\n- Instead of calling the address being saved a \"home\", or using \"claim\" or \"household\" for it, say \"place\" and \"Only you\" — because claiming is a much heavier promise (the only exception is the claimed-home user's line \"Today still uses your home.\").\n\nDONE WHEN: A signed-in person on any platform can go from \"Add a place\" to the saved address in one sheet, with no dead end, and ends up back where they started with a true sentence about which place Today uses. A typo still finds the address. A failed lookup still saves. A Portland address saves with its layer line. A duplicate needs no retyping. Nobody is surprised by which place Today uses afterwards, including people with a home, a chosen place, or a viewed or pinned location.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 01-suggestions · light — large detent, typo typed, five ranked rows, keyboard up, Save and caption pinned above it, top of Your places dimmed above the sheet.\n2. f1-add-place-sheet · web-1440 · 01-suggestions · light — centred modal over Your places, sidebar visible and dimmed.\n3. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 01-suggestions · light — full-height sheet above the keyboard.\n4. f1-add-place-sheet · web-390 · 01-suggestions · light — bottom sheet, host dimmed above it.\n5. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 02-idle-first-place · light — over Today's no-place card: empty focused field, caption, Save disabled, scope sentence, no switch caption.\n6. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 03-selected · light — Birchfield confirmed, Save enabled, \"Today will switch to this address…\" caption.\n7. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 04-not-found-manual · light — message and the five line-by-line fields, State picker at WA, sheet height unchanged.\n8. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 05-outside-clark-county · light — Portland address with its layer line.\n9. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 06-duplicate · light — Already saved row selected, dated duplicate message with no inline action, primary Use for Today, text button Open it.\n10. f1-add-place-sheet · web-390 · 03b-from-compare-header · light — opened from the compare header, already in the selected state with Birchfield confirmed.\n11. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 07-saving · light — button loading, field locked.\n12. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 08-saved-onto-today · light — opened from Today: Today after dismissal, location row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\" and the status row under it.\n13. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 08b-saved-onto-your-places · light — opened from Your places: Birchfield on top with \"Used for Today\", status line \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" with See Today.\n14. f1-add-place-sheet · web-1440 · 14-has-chosen-place · light — Today after saving, status row \"Saved privately. Today still uses Mom's house, the place you chose.\"\n15. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 15-lookup-service-down · light — manual fields open with the service message.\n16. f1-add-place-sheet · web-390 · 09-offline · light — field and Save disabled with reasons, typed text kept.\n17. f1-add-place-sheet · web-1440 · 10-save-error · light — InlineErrorRow, address kept.\n18. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 11-home-user-saved · light — Maya back on Your places: the new saved row in \"Saved places\", status line \"Saved privately. Today still uses your home.\" with See Today.\n19. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 12-ax5 · light — frame 6 at AX5, scrolling.\n20. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 13-greyscale · light — frame 8 in greyscale.\n21. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 01-suggestions · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n22. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 04-not-found-manual · dark — dark twin of frame 7.\n23. f1-add-place-sheet · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — Notes: assumptions; frames dated Sat 10 Oct (fixture save day) rather than TODAY, and frame 5 is the unnamed signed-in first-place case; fixture note: this project draws Jordan adding Birchfield from Your places at 6:10 PM Sat 10 Oct, while the save and email projects draw him saving it through registration and email confirmation at the same time, for the founder to reconcile; every invented string (the four other suggestions, 408 NE Juniper St, the longest address, the layer line, all status lines including the viewed and pinned variants, the switch caption, the unit field label, the map-placement line, the State default, \"5 addresses found\"); extended duplicate message with date: \"You already saved this as “Mom’s house” on Fri 4 Sep.\" and the row string \"Already saved as Mom's house · Fri 4 Sep\" (the contract's duplicate variant, with its inline action hidden here); new pattern: a post-save status row under Today's location row (bodySmall text.primary, role=status, stays until the person leaves Today), not a contract component, proposed for the Foundations board; departs from doc F1 (Preview an address → /start) per the research change, and f1-today-tab must match; the labels \"Add a place\", \"Save an address first\" and \"Save an address to see today here\" all lead here; omitted states (\"Looking up addresses…\" drawn only as copy; the map-placement status; the home-user duplicate with \"Open it\"; the viewed and pinned status lines); the rule that home users are not offered Use for Today, pending the resolver question in Your places.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-23.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Success now returns to the opening screen: onto Today from Today/widget/place file/compare header, onto Your places (new top row plus status line with See Today) from Your places; added artboard 08b; frame 17 (now 18) shows Maya back on Your places (review major).",
          "Added viewed-location and pinned-location status variants with no switch caption; added to COPY, EDGE CASES and Notes (review major; doc §3 resolver order).",
          "Duplicate: board's curly quotes used, inline 'Use for Today' action hidden in the duplicate state, dated message recorded on Notes as an extension of the contract variant (review minors).",
          "Chosen-place artboard now quotes the full 'Saved privately. …' string (review minor).",
          "Notes record the departure from doc F1 'Preview an address → /start'; added 'Save an address first' widget how-to as an entry point (review minor; flows-spec flow-07).",
          "Restored v1 rules: sheet keeps its height when a state replaces the list; INSTEAD OF line against a /start link (review minor).",
          "Added founder-reconcile fixture note; renamed 'anonymous first-place case' to 'unnamed signed-in first-place case' (review minors).",
          "Fixed dim-host instruction per platform so it no longer conflicts with full-height sheets (review minor).",
          "ATTACH adds Today warming-state backdrops and Maya's Your places backdrop (review minor).",
          "'5 addresses found' added to COPY and Notes; post-save status row recorded as a new pattern proposed for Foundations (review minor).",
          "Added focus-after-save note and ONE JOB wording updated to cover returning to origin."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f1-save-confirmation",
        "name": "Saved — Today now uses this address",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 18,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Saved — Today now uses this address · f1-save-confirmation\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Keep this address handy\", the pending-place confirmation. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. On web it becomes the success state of the save on the Place tab, inside the Place shell, not a separate page. On iOS and Android it stays the screen it already is.\n\nATTACH: (1) the current \"Keep this address handy\" screen on iOS and Android; (2) a web capture of it at 1440 and 390; (3) the /start sticky save bar reading \"Keep this address handy\", for continuity; (4) Today's location row with the \"Saved place · Only you\" chip; (5) the Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915 · web 1440x900 (Place shell with the sidebar, content column 560 wide) · web 390x844 (four-tab bar).\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab, the save moment just before Today. Entry points:\n(1) /start → \"Keep this address handy\" → register: lands on 03-saved, because the address was saved at registration. /start → \"Keep this address handy\" → sign in: the save runs on arrival, showing 02-saving only if it takes 1s or longer, then 03-saved. The person never taps Save twice. The native launch funnel works the same way.\n(2) The email confirmation page, whose code or link opens 03-saved directly with \"Email confirmed.\" as a status line at the top, never the pre-save Save button, because the person already asked to keep the address.\n(3) Recovery arrivals: when the /start draft is lost or expired on arrival, or the person confirms their email after the hold has expired (held mode), this screen opens in recovery: 04a when the server or this device still has the address, otherwise 04b. The email page does not draw its own recovery; it routes here.\nThe Add a place sheet does not open this screen: it reuses this screen's saved sentence as a status line. The previous step hands over the address the server holds (the device's own copy is only a backup, not the normal cross-device path) and the account it was started under. Where actions lead: See Today goes to Today in its warming state, location row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\". Claim this address opens the existing claim flow. See your places opens Your places. This screen never asks for notification permission.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Jordan Lee looked up 1107 NE Birchfield Ct on his work laptop at lunch on Sat 10 Oct, the day after moving from Portland, and registered. At 6:10 PM that day he confirms his email on his iPhone and arrives here. These frames are dated Sat 10 Oct, the fixture save day.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Say in one sentence what the save changed, then hand the person to Today.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the title \"Saved privately\" with its tick, then on the one sentence naming what changed, then on the filled \"See Today\" button, the single primary action.\n\nCONTENT:\nPre-save (01): title \"Keep this address handy\"; address line \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\"; body \"Today and a night-before pickup reminder run on it.\"; primary \"Save\"; caption \"Only you will see this.\"\nSaving (02): actions disabled, address intact, and the inline line \"Saving…\" only if the save takes 1s or longer.\nSaved (03): title \"Saved privately\" with a tick; the same address line; body \"Today now uses this address, and so will any reminders you turn on.\"; primary \"See Today\"; secondary \"Claim this address\" with caption \"A separate step, only if you live here.\"; tertiary \"See your places\"; caption under the stack \"Only you will see this.\" When arriving from the email page, a status line \"Email confirmed.\" sits above the title. This is the exact page the email project draws as its confirmed landing; there is no separate \"Saved … to your account.\" line (flow-01 step 8's line is folded into the title plus the address line).\nAnnounced on save: \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\"\nRecovery, address still held on the server or on this device (04a): keep the pre-save title. Body \"Save the address you looked up?\" Then the AddressChip selectable recovery row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\", a text button \"Different address\", and the caption \"Only you will see this.\"\nRecovery, nothing held anywhere (04b): keep the pre-save title. Body \"We stopped holding that address. Type it again to save it.\" Then a blank, focused \"Street address\" field, the button \"Save it\" and the caption.\nStorage error (05, web only): \"We couldn't save that. Your browser blocked the storage we use to hold it.\" with \"Try again\"; the address stays shown.\nSave failed (05b, all platforms): an InlineErrorRow under the address: \"We couldn't save that. Try again.\" with \"Try again\"; the address stays shown.\nAccount switched (06): \"This preview was started on a different account, so we didn't save it.\" Primary \"Preview it on this account\"; text button \"Switch account\". Saved-at-registration version of 06: \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct is saved to the account that registered. We didn't save anything to this account.\" with primary \"Switch account\" and no \"Preview it on this account\".\nOffline (07): the saved state from cache, with \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\". See Today and See your places stay enabled (your places open from cache). Claim this address is disabled with the reason \"You're offline. Claiming needs a connection.\"\nHome variant (Maya, HOME A, saves 1107 NE Birchfield Ct): body \"Today keeps using your home, 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.\" Primary \"See your places\"; tertiary \"See Today\"; no Claim button.\nChosen-place variant (Jordan had picked Mom's house with Use for Today): body \"Today still uses Mom's house, the place you chose.\"\nViewed-location variant (Today runs on a location he looked at recently that is not a saved place): body \"Today still uses the location you looked at recently.\" Pinned twin: \"Today still uses the location you pinned.\"\nDuplicate: the AddressChip duplicate variant showing only its message \"You already saved this as “Mom’s house”\" (its inline action hidden); primary \"Use for Today\"; if it is already Today's place, primary \"See Today\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: A title that switches between two states, with one small tick glyph in primary.700 at body size beside the saved title, and nothing more. Show the address once, as a single line under the title: not a card, and not repeated in the body. Stack the three actions full width in strict weight order: filled primary, outlined secondary, plain-text tertiary. \"Only you will see this.\" is a caption under the stack, never a second paragraph. 01-pre-save is the host's existing before state; it appears only when the person arrives without having already asked to keep the address, for example in the native launch funnel before its Keep tap. The recovery frames keep the pre-save title and swap only the body, so a lost address reads as \"pick it or type it\", not an error page: no error red, no warning glyph, no illustration. The held row always wins; the blank field appears only when nothing is held anywhere. When data is missing, the address line never goes blank; it falls back to a recovery frame.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Save swaps the title with a cross-fade of 200ms or less; the tick appears still, with no animated check. iOS and Android give one light haptic tick on the saved state. Saving disables the actions and shows \"Saving…\" only if the save takes 1s or longer. \"Save it\" on the held row saves in one tap and lands on 03-saved. \"Different address\" swaps the row for the field in place. See Today with no session (for example a mail app's in-app browser) opens Today after sign-in and keeps the saved address. With Reduce Motion on, every swap is instant.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: AddressChip (selectable recovery row; duplicate variant with its inline action hidden; always paired with the ScopeChip sentence) · ScopeChip (sentence form \"Only you will see this.\") · InlineErrorRow (save-failed variant, value kept) · OfflineNotice with FreshnessLine (offline variant).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: The saved confirmation, \"Saving…\" and \"Email confirmed.\" are role=status, announced without moving focus. On arrival from an email link, focus starts on the title. Reading order: status line, title, address, sentence, See Today, Claim this address, its caption, See your places, scope caption. The tick is decorative; the title carries the meaning. The held row is one element with a 44pt / 48dp / 44px target that reads \"Save 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas\". Buttons are 44pt / 48dp / 44px. A disabled Claim stays focusable and reads its reason. At AX5 the address and sentence wrap, and nothing truncates.\n\nCOPY: \"Keep this address handy\" · \"Today and a night-before pickup reminder run on it.\" · \"Save\" · \"Saving…\" · \"Saved privately\" · \"Email confirmed.\" · \"Today now uses this address, and so will any reminders you turn on.\" · \"See Today\" · \"Claim this address\" · \"A separate step, only if you live here.\" · \"See your places\" · \"Only you will see this.\" · \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" · \"Save the address you looked up?\" · \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\" · \"Different address\" · \"We stopped holding that address. Type it again to save it.\" · \"Street address\" · \"Save it\" · \"We couldn't save that. Your browser blocked the storage we use to hold it.\" · \"We couldn't save that. Try again.\" · \"Try again\" · \"This preview was started on a different account, so we didn't save it.\" · \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct is saved to the account that registered. We didn't save anything to this account.\" · \"Preview it on this account\" · \"Switch account\" · \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" · \"You're offline. Claiming needs a connection.\" · \"Today keeps using your home, 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.\" · \"Today still uses Mom's house, the place you chose.\" · \"Today still uses the location you looked at recently.\" · \"Today still uses the location you pinned.\" · \"You already saved this as “Mom’s house”\" · \"Use for Today\" · \"Flood, wildfire, air and radon readings work here. Pickup days and local deadlines are on file only in Clark County, WA for now.\"\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest address, \"12808 NE Lacamas Shores Rd, Unit 204, Camas, WA 98607\", wraps to two lines. An address outside Clark County adds the layer line under the address. An already-saved address shows the duplicate variant. A mail app's in-app browser with no cookies still lands on 03-saved, never on a sign-in page; See Today there goes through sign-in and keeps the address. A confirm after the hold expired lands on 04a or 04b, never on 03-saved. A slow save never shows a full-page spinner. A save failure keeps the address and offers Try again. A claimed-home user gets the home variant. A person with a chosen place, or whose Today runs on a viewed or pinned location, gets the matching \"still uses\" body. A different signed-in account gets 06, which must visibly refuse to save; in saved-at-registration mode its only primary is Switch account.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of confetti, an animated check, a full-bleed illustration or \"Congratulations\", draw one still tick and one factual sentence — because a quiet acknowledgement is what people trust.\n- Instead of \"Set up a Home\" as primary, keep See Today primary and Claim this address secondary — because Today is where the value is, and claiming is optional.\n- Instead of a field when the server or this device holds the address, draw the one-tap held row — because nobody should retype what we hold.\n- Instead of landing on the pre-save Save button after sign-in or registration, land on the saved state — because the person already asked to keep the address.\n- Instead of a notification ask or \"Turn on reminders\" here, say only what changed — because permission is asked later, after a pickup day is confirmed.\n- Instead of dead-end error pages for recovery or account switch, keep the title and give one clear next action — because the person is one tap from done.\n- Instead of wording that implies a home was created or anyone was told, say \"Saved privately\" and \"Only you\" — because a saved place grants nothing and nobody else sees it.\n- Instead of \"Today now uses this address\" when a chosen place, a home, or a viewed or pinned location stays in charge, name what Today still uses — because the sentence must be true.\n\nDONE WHEN: Someone who registered on a laptop and confirmed on a phone sees \"Saved privately\" with the address and taps See Today, with nothing to retype and no second Save tap. The one sentence names what changed, truthfully. There is no celebration and no permission ask. The recovery frames look like the happy path, not like errors, and the email project's confirmed landing matches 03-saved exactly.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 03-saved · light — \"Email confirmed.\" line, title, tick, address, sentence, three actions (See Today, Claim this address, See your places), captions.\n2. f1-save-confirmation · web-1440 · 03-saved · light — inside the Place shell with the sidebar.\n3. f1-save-confirmation · android · 03-saved · light — same content as frame 1.\n4. f1-save-confirmation · web-390 · 03-saved · light — four-tab bar.\n5. f1-save-confirmation · web-1440 · 01-pre-save · light — Keep this address handy, Save (host's before state).\n6. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 02-saving · light — actions disabled, \"Saving…\", address intact.\n7. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 04a-recovery-held · light — held row plus Different address.\n8. f1-save-confirmation · android · 04b-recovery-nothing-held · light — blank focused field plus Save it.\n9. f1-save-confirmation · web-390 · 05-storage-error · light — web only.\n10. f1-save-confirmation · android · 05b-save-failed · light — InlineErrorRow under the address, Try again.\n11. f1-save-confirmation · web-1440 · 06-account-switched · light — refusal line, Preview it on this account, Switch account.\n12. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 07-offline · light — cached saved state, See Today and See your places enabled, Claim disabled with its reason.\n13. f1-save-confirmation · android · 08-home-user-saved · light — Maya's variant.\n14. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 09-ax5 · light — frame 1 at AX5.\n15. f1-save-confirmation · android · 10-greyscale · light — frame 3 in greyscale.\n16. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 03-saved · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n17. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 04a-recovery-held · dark — dark twin of frame 7.\n18. f1-save-confirmation · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — Notes: assumptions; frames dated Sat 10 Oct (fixture save day); every invented string (the saved body sentence, the Claim caption, \"Saving…\", the recovery lines, Switch account, the saved-at-registration 06 line, the offline reason, the home-variant, chosen-place, viewed and pinned sentences, the longest address); the arrival rule: register lands on 03-saved, sign-in runs the save on arrival, and 01-pre-save appears only when the person has not yet asked to keep the address; the recovery routing: a lost or expired draft and a confirm after the hold expired open 04a or 04b here, and the email project routes to them; flow-01 step 8's \"Saved … to your account.\" is folded into \"Saved privately\" plus the address line; \"View saved places\" is renamed \"See your places\" to name its destination (f1-your-places entry updated to match); the duplicate chip shows its message only because the primary carries Use for Today; that the home variant's action order and its missing Claim button are assumptions; that See Today with no session goes through sign-in and keeps the address; that the inventory lists the Add a place sheet as an entry but this prompt follows f1-add-place-sheet, which shows the saved sentence as its own status line; omitted states, drawn only as copy (chosen-place, viewed, pinned and duplicate variants; the saved-at-registration 06 variant with Switch account as primary; the outside-Clark-County layer line).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Aligned 03-saved with the email handoff: no 'Saved … to your account.' line; Notes record that flow-01 step 8's line is folded into the title plus address (review major + minor).",
          "Stated which arrivals open 04a/04b (lost/expired draft, confirm after hold expired) and that the email page routes here rather than drawing its own recovery (review major; flows-spec failure branch and handoff gap).",
          "Rewrote entry (1): register lands on 03-saved; sign-in saves on arrival via 02-saving; never a second Save tap; 01-pre-save limited to arrivals that have not asked to keep the address; recorded on Notes; INSTEAD OF added (review major).",
          "Added viewed-location and pinned body variants (review minor).",
          "Offline keeps See your places enabled; reason now 'You're offline. Claiming needs a connection.' (review minor; matches f1-your-places offline frame).",
          "Added 'Saving…' string; held-row target now 44pt / 48dp / 44px (review minor).",
          "Saved-at-registration 06 gets primary 'Switch account' and no Preview button; it and the outside-Clark-County layer line listed as omitted states on Notes (review minor).",
          "Duplicate chip shows message only with curly quotes; inline action hidden (review minor).",
