                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "Two frames have impossible timelines. (a) Frame 11 dates HOME A's verification before the claim and before a date on which the prompt says the address is still unverified. (b) Frame 9 has PLACE B's postcard mailed three days before the prompt says the place was saved. It also shows a Proof row at T1, which contradicts the prompt's own T1 rules.",
                    "evidence": "prompts x-place-file: \"Claimed Sat 17 Oct … The address is not verified yet.\" (as of Mon 19 Oct), but frame 11 has \"“Confirmed by postcard · Thu 15 Oct 2026”\". T1: \"a person who saved PLACE B on Sat 17 Oct\", but Postcard copy has \"Postcard mailed Wed 14 Oct\" and frame 9 is \"PLACE B, claim in progress, Proof row pending\". T1 rules: \"Proof has no section until something is known\" and \"Money, people and proof · Not here — this is a saved place\". flows-spec flow-06 step 2–3 puts the postcard request inside the claim flow.",
                    "fix": "Frame 11: give it its own as-of date after Mon 19 Oct, and date the verification after the claim (e.g. “Address confirmed by postcard · Mon 26 Oct 2026”). Frame 9: move the postcard dates after Sat 17 Oct (e.g. mailed Tue 20 Oct · expected Mon 26 Oct–Mon 2 Nov · code expires Thu 19 Nov · new code after Mon 2 Nov). State that in this frame a pending Proof row replaces the grey “Money, people and proof · Not here” row for Proof. List both changes on Notes."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt drops the voter-registration self-report state and its honesty rules. “I did this” must read “You marked this done”, stay Only you (never shown to the household), and say the app cannot check registration status. Frame 3 (Sam's view) makes this a real privacy question.",
                    "evidence": "ux-research-brief §6: \"Never state or imply registration status. 'I did this' reads 'You marked this done' and stays Only you.\" derive-proposals f6-just-moved-card-synced: \"Self-report receipt under the register row once ticked: 'You told us you did this on {date}. We can't check registration status.'\" flows-spec flow-13 step 6: \"The self-report is never shown to the household as a fact.\" The prompt draws only “Forward your mail” in the done state, and the voter mover row and voter DateRow have no done or visibility rule.",
                    "fix": "Add to JUST MOVED: once ticked, the ‘Update your voter registration’ row reads “You marked this done Sat 17 Oct · We can't check registration status” with the person glyph + “Only you”. Add to EDGE CASES/member view: Maya's voter self-report is never shown in Sam's view, and Sam's own row is independent."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The promoted asks have no decline. The research requires every first-week ask to pair “Not now” with a lasting decline that is stored on the server, can be undone, and has a way back in. The FactRow ‘declined’ variant is listed but no row, copy or frame uses it.",
                    "evidence": "ux-research-brief §2.7: \"Every ask pairs 'Not now' (never shown again automatically) with a lasting decline ('Just me', 'Skip', 'No thanks'). The decline is stored on the server, can be undone, and has a way back through a place-file row or settings.\" derive-proposals f7-add-widget-nudge: \"with a dismiss affordance\". The prompt's widget row and \"When does your home insurance renew? · Add a date\" have no decline, and only the “Set up your place” block has a Dismiss.",
                    "fix": "Give each promoted ask a neutral, equal-weight decline (e.g. widget row “Not now”; insurance ask “Skip”). A decline collapses the row to an InlineUndo (“Hid 'Put today on your home screen' · Undo”) and moves the ask into “More you can add”. Add the FactRow declined state to a frame (e.g. frame 4 or 17) and list the strings on Notes."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The keeper re-entry row is missing. This is a must-adopt per-surface change, and the research says Skip closes the Today slot so the place file is the way back. The prompt only draws the named ‘Ollie’ state.",
                    "evidence": "per-surface-changes: \"Add persistent rows: … 'Give your place a keeper' (re-entry after Skip)\". ux-research-brief P21: \"Skip closes the slot, and it can be reopened from the place file.\" flows-spec flow-09 failure branch: \"She can come back through a Place-section row in the place file or through Settings.\" The prompt only has \"Keeper · “Ollie” (phase 2).\"",
                    "fix": "Add a Place row variant: “Give your place a keeper” (quiet FactRow, text action, opens the keeper naming sheet), shown when no keeper is named or after Skip. It is phase 2 and absent until the feature ships. Draw it in the T1 frame or on Notes, and never as a promoted ask."
                  },
                  {
