                    "issue": "The widget row is missing its research-backed behaviour. The prompt omits the Android pin API path, the once-per-24h limit, and how the app knows a widget is placed, so it cannot hide the row. The critique flagged that last gap specifically.",
                    "evidence": "per-surface-changes: \"The widget row offers the Android pin API or the iOS how-to, at most once per 24h\". derive-proposals f7-add-widget-nudge: \"Suppressed automatically once a widget is placed (iOS WidgetCenter.getCurrentConfigurations, Android AppWidgetManager.getAppWidgetIds …) and while the user has no place\". flows-spec flow-07 step 12: \"a snapshot read or a pin callback\". The prompt only says \"If the widget is already placed, the widget row is gone\".",
                    "fix": "Add: on Android the row opens the how-to sheet, whose main button is “Add to home screen” (requestPinAppWidget); iOS opens the how-to sheet with the user's own preview. The row is offered at most once per 24h after a dismissal. It hides when the app detects a placed widget (iOS WidgetCenter configurations / Android AppWidgetManager ids or pin callback). It is also hidden when there is no place. Note this on frame 17."
                  },
