                    "issue": "The design reasoning behind the merge was dropped. This screen replaces four lists (first-week checklist, Just Moved card, Your dates card, keeper ledger) that had four storage models and four dismissals. It is also the only place a date more than 14 days out can be seen and deleted. v1 marked this reasoning “do not optimise this away”, and nothing in v2 stops a designer from drawing the sections back as separate card styles.",
                    "evidence": "prompts-v1: \"WHY IT IS SHAPED THIS WAY (do not optimise this away): the same facts are today drawn as four different lists … with four storage models and four dismissals. This is the merge. … a lease ending eight months from now is currently saved, toasted, then invisible until two weeks before it fires.\" The inventory uxNote says the same. v2 has no equivalent section.",
                    "fix": "Add a short WHY section: “This one list replaces the first-week checklist, the Just Moved card, the Your dates card and the keeper ledger. Draw every section with the same FactRow/DateRow grammar and one dismissal pattern, not as separate cards. It is the only place a date beyond 14 days can be seen, edited and deleted, and it gives a saved-place user a reason to open the Place tab.”"
