                    "evidence": "Prompt: \"12 month columns of 22pt on iOS and web 390\"; \"one XS ProvenanceMark, plus a count numeral when there are 2 or more\"; \"the month cell of the city lane shows the moved mark next to a struck ghost mark\"; contract ProvenanceMark: \"XS 12pt/dp, the smallest size at which the three shapes must still be told apart\"",
                    "fix": "Specify the phone cell geometry: \"Lanes are 28pt tall. In a phone month cell, marks stack vertically (at most 2 rows). A holiday move is the moved mark on top and the struck 12pt ghost below it. A count sits below its single mark as a caption numeral ('2'), never beside it. On phones the city-lane rhythm is a 2pt tick per service week (not marks), with a solid tick for confirmed weeks and a dashed tick for projected ones; the month's mark sits above the ticks.\" Add a zoomed Notes inset of the Nov city cell at 22pt."
