      {
        "ids": [
          "f1-today-tab",
          "f5-today-calendar-strip"
        ],
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f1-today-tab",
            "name": "Today (one composition, both payloads)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 23,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Today · f1-today-tab\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Today\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. What changes: three screens are called Today today (the Today tab, Place › Today, and a briefing screen that only a push can open). Merge them into ONE composition per platform. Reuse the existing cards as drawn. Change only their order, when they show, and their states.\n\nATTACH: (1) the current Today tab on web /app/today at 1440 and 390, on iOS and on Android; (2) web Place › Today (/app/place/today): its \"Next 14 days at this address\" card and its \"Good day to…\" tiles move into this tab; (3) the iOS briefing screen opened from a push; (4) the Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393×852 (primary; large title \"Today\"). Android 412×915 (Material 3 top app bar). Web 1440×900: left sidebar and one centred content column 720 wide, so the reading order stays the same. Web 390×844 with the bottom tab bar. Draw artboards 01, 02, 04, 13, 14, 19, 20, 21 and 22 as full-length scrolls at their platform width (as tall as the content), with a dashed line at the fold. Draw all other artboards at their platform viewport: iOS 393×852, Android 412×915, web 1440×900 and 390×844. The web and Android dense frames (16–18) may also be drawn full-length with a dashed fold line.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: the Today tab, second of Place · Today · Nearby · Mail. Entry points:\n- The tab itself: bottom bar (phones, web 390) or left sidebar (web 1440). Web URL /app/today. /app/place/today (including ?rule=…) redirects here with its query intact.\n- A briefing push: pantopus://hub-today?deliveryId=…&kind=morning|evening. The evening briefing (6:00 PM) carries pickup and next-day items; the morning briefing (7:00 AM) carries date items. Either one opens this tab, hands over the delivered items, fills the pinned slot by rule (b) below, and highlights the matching section.\n- An air or NOAA alert push: pantopus://today?section=air&src=alert. It fills the pinned slot for Today's place. An alert for a different saved place lands on the air band screen (f1-today-air-band) for that place, not on this tab.\n- A widget tap: pantopus://today?src=widget&section=pickup|strip|air. Content already on screen stays; Today scrolls to that section and highlights it once.\n- A date reminder push: pantopus://today?rule=… or /app/today?rule=…. Today scrolls to that row in the 14-day card (f5 draws the row), then the DateSheet opens in view mode. If the date is outside the 14 days, the link opens the place file's Dates row instead (x-place-file); Today is not the landing. A removed date shows \"That date was removed.\" as a status line under the 14-day card's summary.\n- \"See Today\" on the save confirmation. Today arrives warming, and the location row already shows the new saved place.\n- The first open after claiming an address or joining a household shows a one-time notice.\n- Removing the last saved place returns here in the no-place state. A briefing push tapped after its place was removed also lands in the no-place state.\nOut of Today: the location-row chip opens Your places. FirstWeekRow scrolls to and highlights the control that holds its step. Strip rows and \"+ Add a date\" open the DateSheet. \"Add a place\" opens the add-place sheet. The one-time claim notice opens the claim receipt.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: At 6:10 PM Mon 19 Oct, Maya Chen opens Today at HOME A before she wheels the carts out. Jordan Lee opens Today at PLACE B out of habit with notifications never turned on; nothing is due tomorrow there. (Delta) For this project Jordan saved PLACE B on Sat 17 Oct, 2 days before TODAY, so he is inside the 7-day first-week window; artboard 03 replays his first open seconds after saving.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: In one scroll, read everything happening at this address today, and see that a quiet day really was checked.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first the location row (address, ScopeChip, FreshnessLine). Second, the pinned slot if it is filled; at a new saved place, FirstWeekRow \"Next: set your pickup day →\", the one next step. Third, the PickupCard (or QuietDayReceipt), then the 14-day card. Today is for reading, so it has no page-level primary button. The only action is the one inside the top card, or FirstWeekRow during the first week.\n\nCONTENT (fixtures plus these deltas):\n- HOME A location row: \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" · ScopeChip \"Your household\" · \"Updated 4m ago\". PLACE B: \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" · \"Saved place · Only you\".\n- PickupCard at HOME A, as f4-today-pickup-card draws its confirmed variant: \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\" · \"Bins out tonight — curbside by 6:30 AM\" · \"You · Tuesday · Waste Connections\" with the you-added mark.\n- 14-day card, as f5 draws it: \"Next 14 days: 4 items\" (Tue 20 pickup, Mon 26 statewide voter bar, Tue 27 garbage only, Sun 1 Nov HOA dues added by Sam). Artboards 04 and 05 use f5's 6-item strip (f5 artboard 02: \"Next 14 days: 6 items\", which adds the Tue 20 bulk pickup and Maya's renters-insurance row).\n- Weather (delta): \"54°F · Dry tonight · Rain from Wed morning\" · \"National Weather Service · Portland forecast office · updated 5:45 PM\".\n- Air, as f1-today-air-band draws it: section title \"Air quality index (AQI)\", AqiBand detail \"AQI 42 · Good · PM2.5\", the EPA Good statement, \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\".\n- Alerts: none, so the section takes no space.\n- Ranked signal (delta): KindGlyph property-tax · \"Pay property tax, 2nd half\" · \"in 14 days · due Mon 2 Nov\" · detail \"For property owners in Clark County · moved from Sat 31 Oct\" · \"Clark County Treasurer · county-wide\". The mark follows the seeded rule's confidence: draw it official only because this project assumes the seed was checked against the Treasurer; an unchecked seed shows the hollow mark.\n- Tile (delta): \"Good day to clear the gutters — dry until Wednesday\".\n- Briefing opt-in card at HOME A: the morning row reads \"7:00 AM · Change\" and the night-before row reads \"6:00 PM · Change\". At PLACE B it has never asked (artboard 02) or was declined (artboard 06).\n- PLACE B only: FirstWeekRow \"Next: set your pickup day →\" and QuietDayReceipt, each CheckItem with its source time: \"weather 5:45 PM · air 7:00 AM · alerts 6:00 PM · your calendar 6:00 PM\". The gutters tile shows, and the property-tax signal shows below the receipt: it is a heads-up 14 days out, below the push threshold, so it does not cancel the all-clear.\n- Alert variant: AQI 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, crossed at 4:00 PM, Maya's threshold 101.\n- Worst case (artboard 04): the full label \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\" wraps to two lines beside the chip and \"Updated 2h ago\", with the pinned alert, the PickupCard and f5's 6-item strip below.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: Draw this vertical order, the same at every tier and on every platform:\n1 location row · 2 pinned slot · 2b FirstWeekRow (first 7 days only; zero height when complete or hidden) · 3 PickupCard (on a quiet day, QuietDayReceipt takes this slot) · 4 14-day card · 4b keeper slot (phase 2; zero height in this project, and hidden whenever an alert is pinned) · 5 weather · 6 AqiBand · 7 alerts · 8 ranked signals · 9 \"Good day to…\" tiles · 10 briefing opt-in card.\nEach section title is an accessibility heading. A section appears or vanishes with its data, and the sections that stay never move. Claiming an address must read as \"the chip changed, and any household sections appeared\". Whenever a place exists, the 14-day card never disappears.\nThe pinned slot holds at most one card, in this precedence for every arrival type:\n(a) An active air or NOAA crossing at Today's place: the AqiBand widget-micro variant (name and number beside the track, no text on fills) with \"Air quality index (AQI) 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\", \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM · AirNow\" and \"See air quality ↓\". A NOAA crossing uses the same form: \"Wind advisory until 10:00 PM Tue\" · \"National Weather Service · Portland forecast office\" · \"See alerts ↓\".\n(b) On a briefing-push arrival, list only the delivered items that are NOT in the first viewport, headed \"From your 6:00 PM briefing · Also:\" (morning: \"From your 7:00 AM briefing · Also:\") with one \"↓\" line each, each scrolling to and highlighting its row. Highlight any delivered item that is already in the first viewport in place; never repeat it in the slot. If every item is in the first viewport, the slot takes no space.\n(c) The one-time claim or join notice, drawn with LandingBannerSlot geometry.\n(d) Otherwise it takes no space.\nQuiet day: draw a finished screen, not an empty state. Show the heading only when all four CheckItems are ticked.\nWarming: for cold loads over 1s only, draw WarmingSkeleton section shapes at final height in slots 3–6. Each fills in as its provider returns. While warming, the FreshnessLine under the address reads \"Setting up Today for Birchfield Ct\"; it becomes \"Updated just now\" once every provider has returned or timed out. After 10s, a provider that still hasn't returned becomes its InlineErrorRow (\"We couldn't reach AirNow just now · Retry\"); the others stay as they landed. FirstWeekRow shows during warming. Warm refresh: never skeleton or dim anything. The FreshnessLine reads \"Updating…\" then \"Updated just now\", with the hairline only if the refresh takes 1s or longer.\nHidden details (the address resolves but weather, air, alerts, signals and tiles are withheld): show the hidden-details line directly above slot 3, full width, in bodySmall text.strong on surface.sunken; the PickupCard (when pickup is tomorrow) and the 14-day card follow in their usual slots.\nWhen data is missing: a failed provider gets an InlineErrorRow in its own slot. A refresh failure keeps the content. With no cache, show the error state. Offline, show cached content with OfflineNotice, and each disabled control carries its reason caption.\nSignals never repeat a section's fact. Pickup appears once, as the PickupCard with its KindGlyph, never with a sparkle icon.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: On an arrival from a push, widget or reminder, scroll once to the target and highlight it with the DateRow highlighted wash (fades in under 300ms, then decays); accessibility focus moves there. If a push arrives while Today is open, show no banner; highlight the PickupCard, and the notification bell badge increments; nothing else changes.\nFirstWeekRow: the step order is Save ✓ → Pickup day → Reminder or widget → One date or person. The row names only the next unfinished step, with no fraction. It is a whole-row link that scrolls to and highlights the control for that step: (1) pickup day: the PickupCard when it is on screen; otherwise the first \"Pickup day\" row's \"Set your pickup day\" button in the 14-day card (f5 draws it); (2) reminder: \"Next: get a reminder the night before →\" scrolls to and highlights the briefing opt-in card in slot 10, whose widget line covers the widget half; (3) date or person: \"Next: add one date that matters →\" highlights the 14-day card's \"+ Add a date\" row; at a claimed home the person half, \"Next: add someone to your household →\", opens the household block in the place file. At a saved place the person half is not offered and not counted; only steps reachable at the current tier count. The row shows for 7 days from the save and disappears when the reachable set is done or when hidden. Its separate 44pt text button \"Hide this\" collapses the row to InlineUndo \"Hidden · Undo\", stored on the server, kept until the person leaves Today; later sections move up once. A member who joined a household never sees FirstWeekRow.\nPull to refresh on native; its alternatives are Retry in the FreshnessLine and a \"Refresh\" accessibility action, and web refreshes on focus. Sections fill in with a 200ms cross-fade. Under Reduce Motion: jump-scroll without animation, a static highlight that clears on the next interaction, no shimmer. Today fires no haptics of its own (the PickupCard confirm has its own).\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ScopeChip (saved place; claimed home; person glyph + \"Only you\" on a private row), FreshnessLine (fresh, refreshing, warming, stale, failed, offline), OfflineNotice, WarmingSkeleton (section skeleton), QuietDayReceipt (Today full: all ticked, one pending, one failed; CheckItems with source times), InlineErrorRow (provider unreachable), PickupCard (confirmed incl. the named-person form, highlighted on arrival), FourteenDayStrip with DateRow (Today card), AqiBand (detail, alert, widget micro in the pinned slot), ProvenanceMark, SourceCaption, KindGlyph, FirstWeekRow (no-fraction variant; dismissed with InlineUndo), InlineUndo, NotificationAsk (card row: never asked, granted, declined), KeeperStrip (slot only, suppressed under an alert), LandingBannerSlot (one-time claim receipt banner variant, used in Today's pinned slot for both notices; the join notice wraps to two lines with \"See your places\" as the trailing 44pt action and a 44pt Close glyph labelled \"Dismiss\").\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order follows the visual order. Each section title is an accessibility heading (web h2), so the VoiceOver rotor, TalkBack headings and web heading navigation jump between sections. The location row is one element, \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop, visible to your household, updated 4 minutes ago\", with custom actions \"Open your places\" and, when refresh failed, \"Retry\". On web, the chip and Retry stay separate 44px buttons after the address text. The receipt is read as \"Checked: weather, air, alerts, your calendar\". The pinned-slot card has role=status on appearance. On iOS the tab bar uses Large Content Viewer. All rows are whole-row targets of at least 44pt / 48dp / 44px, and \"Hide this\" is its own 44pt target. Retry reads \"Retry air quality\". The strip and the air band carry their own summary sentences. At AX5 the location row stacks (address, then chip, then freshness), text wraps, nothing truncates, and the 14-day card shows its summary sentence in place of the cells (the same proposal as f5's AX5 frame). In greyscale, marks read by shape and the AQI by its printed name and separators.\n\nCOPY:\n- \"Today starts with a place\" · \"Save an address and Today will show its weather, air, alerts and dates.\" · primary \"Add a place\" · tertiary link \"Claim an address\"\n- Hidden details (delta): \"Today's details aren't available for this address yet. Your dates and pickup day still show below.\"\n- Warming (delta): \"Setting up Today for Birchfield Ct\"\n- \"Nothing needs your attention today\" · \"Checked 6:00 PM · weather · air · alerts · your calendar\"\n- \"Couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\" · \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" · \"Retry\"\n- \"Updating…\" · \"Updated just now\" · \"Updated 4m ago\" · \"Updated 2h ago\" · \"Couldn't refresh · Retry\"\n- \"You're offline · as of 4:10 PM\" · \"You're offline. Today shows what we had at 4:10 PM.\" (delta) · \"Couldn't load today.\" · \"Retry\"\n- Offline reasons (delta): \"Changing your pickup day needs a connection.\" (PickupCard) · \"Adding a date needs a connection.\" (14-day card) · \"Changing briefing times needs a connection.\" (briefing card)\n- Pinned briefing (delta): \"From your 6:00 PM briefing · Also:\" · \"From your 7:00 AM briefing · Also:\" · \"Renters insurance renews tomorrow ↓\"\n- Pinned alert: \"Air quality index (AQI) 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\" · \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM · AirNow\" · \"See air quality ↓\"; NOAA (delta): \"Wind advisory until 10:00 PM Tue\" · \"See alerts ↓\"\n- One-time notices (delta): \"Birchfield Ct is now your home · See what moved\" · \"Today now uses Larkspur Loop because you joined this household.\" · action \"See your places\" · \"Dismiss\"\n- FirstWeekRow: \"Next: set your pickup day →\" · \"Next: get a reminder the night before →\" (delta) · \"Next: add one date that matters →\" · \"Next: add someone to your household →\" (delta) · \"Hide this\" · \"Hidden · Undo\"\n- Declined notifications, as f4-briefing-optin-card draws it, shown once in that card's slot: \"Pickup still shows here on Today · Or put it on your home screen\"\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest label wraps and never truncates. Largest numbers: AQI 301+ uses the AqiBand's own label; a strip day with more than 3 marks shows \"+N\" (marks not drawn), as f5 draws it. With many saved places, the chip names the one Today uses. A new saved place in its first seconds shows the warming state, never the quiet heading. Tiers: a saved place shows \"Saved place · Only you\" and never shows household copy; a claimed home shows \"Your household\". At a claimed home, a date the viewer kept private shows the ScopeChip person glyph plus \"Only you\" at the end of its SourceCaption line. A household member whose calendar editing the owner has turned off (or a Guest) sees the same order, and the 14-day card has no add row. By default, members such as Sam can add dates. When there is no location, no alert pinned slot ever appears. An alert for a saved place Today does not use (Maya's \"Mom's place\") lands on that place's air band screen, which names it with \"Mom's place · Saved place · Only you\"; Today's pinned slot never shows another place's crossing. A briefing push for a removed place lands in the no-place state. The property-tax signal is county-wide and shows even at a rented home such as HOME A; its detail line says who it applies to.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a full-page spinner while providers load, draw section skeletons in their final slots — because nothing should jump and an all-clear must not show early.\n- Instead of an illustrated \"nothing here yet\" empty state on a quiet day, draw the heading plus four ticked checks with times — because a receipt is what makes silence believable.\n- Instead of \"3 of 6 things on file →\" at the bottom of the page, draw \"Next: set your pickup day →\" directly under the pinned slot — because a fraction reads as percent complete, and a new person needs the next step in view.\n- Instead of moving air or alerts to the top on a bad-air day, fill the pinned slot and link down — because a stable order is learnable and the crossing still sits above the fold.\n- Instead of a pinned briefing line that repeats the PickupCard right under it, highlight the card in place and pin only the items below the fold — because the same fact twice reads as two things.\n- Instead of dropping the chip on a claimed home, show \"Your household\" — because scope is always stated.\n- Instead of \"Today starts with a place\" for anyone who has a location, show the hidden-details line — because it would tell a resident they have no place.\n- Instead of silently switching Today after an invite is accepted, draw the one-time join notice — because an unexplained address change reads as a bug.\n\nDONE WHEN: A new account that saved PLACE B sees weather, air, alerts, the seasonal tile and its calendar in the same order as HOME A, with its one next step above the fold. Artboard 13 differs from artboard 02 only by the chip, the notice, the missing FirstWeekRow step it finished, and any household sections. \"Nothing needs your attention today\" appears only where all four checks are ticked. Someone with notifications off sees the same pickup item a push would carry. Every arrival lands on its exact section, no pinned line repeats a card in the first viewport, and a date outside the window lands in the place file. A member who just joined sees why Today changed and the household's confirmed pickup day, with no first-week asks. The no-place state appears only in the no-place frame. Every frame reads correctly in greyscale.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f1-today-tab · ios · 01-dense-home · light — HOME A at 6:10 PM, organic open, every section with data, no FirstWeekRow (Maya is past her first week), full-length scroll.\n2. f1-today-tab · ios · 02-saved-place-quiet · light — PLACE B with its chip, FirstWeekRow \"Next: set your pickup day →\" with \"Hide this\" at 2b, all-ticked receipt with times, hollow Thursday marks and the \"Set your pickup day\" button in the strip, property-tax signal below the receipt, gutters tile, briefing card never asked, full-length scroll.\n3. f1-today-tab · ios · 03-warming · light — PLACE B seconds after \"See Today\": FreshnessLine \"Setting up Today for Birchfield Ct\", FirstWeekRow, weather landed, other slots skeletons, no heading.\n4. f1-today-tab · ios · 04-alert-pinned · light — worst case: HOME A at AQI 118, two-line label, \"Updated 2h ago\", pinned AqiBand widget-micro summary, PickupCard, f5's 6-item strip, AqiBand alert with the 101 rule, keeper slot hidden, full-length scroll.\n5. f1-today-tab · ios · 05-from-push · light — HOME A after tapping the 6:00 PM briefing: pinned \"From your 6:00 PM briefing · Also: Renters insurance renews tomorrow ↓\", PickupCard highlighted and focused; the 14-day card is f5's 6-item variant (\"Next 14 days: 6 items\"), and the \"↓\" line scrolls to the insurance DateRow and highlights it.\n6. f1-today-tab · ios · 06-partial-airnow · light — PLACE B after declining notifications: AirNow InlineErrorRow in the air slot, a failed CheckItem, no heading, the declined line in the briefing card's slot.\n7. f1-today-tab · ios · 07-from-widget · light — HOME A arriving with section=strip: scrolled to the 14-day card, highlighted, \"Updated just now\".\n8. f1-today-tab · ios · 08-no-place · light — no saved place or home (also the landing for a briefing push whose place was removed).\n9. f1-today-tab · ios · 09-hidden-details · light — location resolved, hidden-details line above slot 3 on surface.sunken, 14-day card still present.\n10. f1-today-tab · ios · 10-refresh-failed · light — all content kept, \"Updated 2h ago · Couldn't refresh · Retry\".\n11. f1-today-tab · ios · 11-offline · light — cached content, OfflineNotice, the three disabled controls each with its reason caption.\n12. f1-today-tab · ios · 12-error · light — no cache, \"Couldn't load today.\" and Retry.\n13. f1-today-tab · ios · 13-after-claim · light — Jordan's first open after claiming Birchfield Ct: the sections of artboard 02 in the same order, chip \"Your household\", LandingBannerSlot notice \"Birchfield Ct is now your home · See what moved\" in the pinned slot, his renters-insurance row ending its SourceCaption with the person glyph and \"Only you\"; full-length scroll.\n14. f1-today-tab · ios · 14-after-join · light — Priya's first open after accepting the HOME A invite: two-line notice \"Today now uses Larkspur Loop because you joined this household.\" with \"See your places\" and \"Dismiss\", chip \"Your household\", PickupCard \"Maya · Tuesday, confirmed 3 Oct 2026\" with the you-added mark shape, no FirstWeekRow (the household's pickup day and dates already count; a joined member is never shown first-week asks); full-length scroll.\n15. f1-today-tab · ios · 15-foreground-push · light — Today already open at 6:00 PM: no banner, PickupCard highlight, bell badge +1.\n16. f1-today-tab · web-1440 · 01-dense-home · light — sidebar plus the 720 column.\n17. f1-today-tab · web-390 · 01-dense-home · light — bottom tab bar.\n18. f1-today-tab · android · 01-dense-home · light — Material 3.\n19. f1-today-tab · ios · 16-ax5 · light — artboard 01 at AX5: location row stacked, text wrapped, strip summary sentence in place of cells; full-length scroll.\n20. f1-today-tab · ios · 17-greyscale · light — artboard 01 in greyscale; full-length scroll.\n21. f1-today-tab · ios · 01-dense-home · dark — dark twin of artboard 01; full-length scroll.\n22. f1-today-tab · ios · 04-alert-pinned · dark — dark twin of artboard 04; full-length scroll.\n23. f1-today-tab · notes — assumptions and every invented string: the weather line, gutters tile, warming line, offline sentence and the three offline reasons, the pinned-briefing lines, the NOAA pinned lines, both notices, \"Next: get a reminder the night before →\", \"Next: add someone to your household →\", \"Hide this\" / \"Hidden · Undo\", \"Claim an address\" (a glossary exception to \"Claim this address\" for the no-place state), Jordan's Sat 17 Oct save date (the fixture says Sat 10 Oct; moved so he is inside the first week), Jordan's claim, Priya's name and acceptance, Maya's confirmation date of 3 Oct 2026, both briefing times being on, and the checked status of the tax seed. Record also: FirstWeekRow sits at 2b; when hidden it collapses to InlineUndo, and later sections move up once. Claimed home shows ScopeChip \"Your household\" (contract and invariant 2); this supersedes \"no chip\" in flow-06 step 8 and the inventory. Contract clarification: LandingBannerSlot is also used in Today's pinned slot. The quiet heading coexists with a below-threshold heads-up signal (property tax, 14 days out). The different-address claim string, not drawn: \"Today now uses Larkspur Loop. Mom's place is still saved.\" (if Maya had earlier saved \"Mom's place · Washougal, WA\"). Open question: whether Today should ever point to an alert at a saved place it does not use (now it does not; the alert lands on that place's air band screen). Place › Today content: the 14-day card and the tiles move here; its sunrise and sunset times are dropped in this project (founder to confirm), and the route only redirects. The keeper slot at 4b, where f11 says \"above the weather, below the pickup card\" (reconcile it there). Omitted states: a location that comes from a pinned viewing location rather than a saved place or home (its chip is not drawn; it must be unaffected by this change), and any other state not drawn.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1–6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7–12, then wait. Turn 3: 13–18, then wait. Turn 4: 19–23.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Pinned slot rule (b) rewritten: pin only delivered items not in the first viewport under 'From your 6:00 PM briefing · Also:', highlight in-view items in place; removed the duplicate 'Recycling and garbage tomorrow ↓' line (review major).",
