          {
            "id": "f5-today-calendar-strip",
            "name": "Next 14 days at this address (strip + rows)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": true,
            "frameCount": 23,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Next 14 days at this address · f5-today-calendar-strip\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Today\" (a new card inside it). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. What changes: the address-calendar list card becomes a FourteenDayStrip card with DateRows beneath it. It sits directly below the PickupCard and above weather.\n\nATTACH: (1) the accepted f1-today-tab frames (ios 01-dense-home, web-1440, android) as the host; (2) the existing \"Next 14 days at this address\" card from web Place › Today and its iOS and Android calendar blocks; (3) the Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393 wide (primary), Android 412 wide, web 1440 (inside Today's 720 column), web 390. Draw each artboard full-length at its platform width: the location row, then the PickupCard collapsed to its top 64pt with a torn-edge marker (or omitted on days without one), then the whole card down to the scope sentence, then 24pt of weather. Put a dashed line at the platform fold (iOS 852, Android 915, web 900 and 844). Never shorten rows to fit.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Today tab → slot 4 of Today. It is always present when a place exists. Entry points:\n- Scrolling Today.\n- A widget tap: pantopus://today?src=widget&section=strip. The card is scrolled into view and highlighted once.\n- A reminder push for a date (pantopus://today?rule=… or /app/today?rule=…; /app/place/today?rule=… redirects here with its query). The row is highlighted and focused, then the DateSheet opens in view mode. If the date is outside the 14 days, the place file's Dates row is the landing instead (drawn in x-place-file). A removed date shows a status line (artboard 13).\n- The place file year band's \"this fortnight\" link.\n- FirstWeekRow on Today: \"Next: add one date that matters →\" scrolls here and highlights the \"+ Add a date\" row. \"Next: set your pickup day →\" (when no PickupCard is on screen) scrolls here and highlights the first \"Pickup day\" row's \"Set your pickup day\" button.\nOut of this card: a row tap opens the DateSheet (view-mine or view-seeded). The row action \"Where this comes from\" swaps the sheet to the ProvenanceSheet content. \"+ Add a date\" opens the DateSheet in create mode. \"Set your pickup day\" opens the DateSheet in create mode with the Pickup day kind. Saving a date inside the window returns here with the new row highlighted; a date outside it returns here with the place-file status line under the summary.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: At 6:10 PM Mon 19 Oct, Maya Chen checks what is coming at HOME A this fortnight: bins tomorrow, the voter deadline, garbage only next week, and the HOA dues Sam entered. Jordan Lee at PLACE B sees two hollow Thursday marks and the renters-insurance date he added, then taps \"+ Add a date\" to add his lease, which ends months away.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: See the next two weeks at this address as a shape, with every item's source and certainty visible without tapping.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first the strip's rhythm (Tuesday marks, the Mon 26 bar). Second, the first row, \"Recycling and garbage · Tomorrow\". Third, the legend. The only primary action is the \"+ Add a date\" row at the foot; at PLACE B, \"Set your pickup day\" is a secondary text button inside its row.\n\nCONTENT (fixtures plus these deltas). Phase-1 kinds only in every artboard except 15. HOME A window Mon 19 Oct → Sun 1 Nov. Summary \"Next 14 days: 4 items\".\n- Tue 20 Oct: \"Recycling and garbage\" · \"Tomorrow\" · \"You · Tuesday · Waste Connections\" · you-added. Two marks in the cell (garbage, recycling).\n- Mon 26 Oct: \"Register or update to vote: online or mail\" · \"in 7 days · must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · \"In person: until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov\" · region chip \"Statewide — WA\" · \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · 2026 general election\" · official. A bar fills the cell.\n- Tue 27 Oct: \"Garbage only\" · \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct\" · you-added. One mark.\n- Sun 1 Nov: \"HOA dues · $285\" · \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" · \"Repeats monthly\" · (delta) entered by Sam: the you-added mark shape with the caption \"Sam added this · 3 Oct\".\n- Many-items deltas (artboard 02, HOME A): Tue 20 Oct also holds \"Bulk pickup — curbside by 6:30 AM\" (official, \"Waste Connections · Vancouver service area · 2026 calendar\") and Maya's \"Renters insurance renews — check the new premium\" (you-added, \"Repeats yearly\"; its title wraps to two lines). The cell shows 3 marks and \"+1\". Summary \"Next 14 days: 6 items\".\n- PLACE B window: Thu 22 Oct and Thu 29 Oct, title \"Pickup day\" · detail \"Which bins go out isn't set yet\" · \"in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" / \"in 10 days · Thu 29 Oct\" · \"City of Camas · weekday only · 2026 calendar\" · on record, not confirmed. The Thu 22 row carries the \"Set your pickup day\" button. Also the Mon 26 Oct bar, and (delta) Jordan's \"Renters insurance renews\" · \"in 11 days · Fri 30 Oct\" · \"Repeats yearly\" · you-added (a tick in the cell). \"Next 14 days: 4 items\".\n- Saved-outside-window delta (artboard 14, PLACE B): Jordan saves \"Lease ends\" on Wed 31 Mar 2027. The card shows, under the summary, the status line \"Saved · Lease ends Wed 31 Mar 2027 is in your place file · See it\"; \"See it\" opens the place file's Dates row. No row is added to the card.\n- Holiday specimen (delta, PLACE B viewed Mon 23 Nov 2026, window Mon 23 Nov → Sun 6 Dec): \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\". The Thu 3 Dec pickup row shows the reported state: \"You reported this · checking\".\n- County specimen (delta, HOME A viewed Tue 20 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM, window Tue 20 Oct → Mon 2 Nov, summary \"Next 14 days: 5 items\"): \"Pay property tax, 2nd half\" · \"in 13 days · due Mon 2 Nov\" · detail \"For property owners in Clark County · moved from Sat 31 Oct\" · region chip \"Clark County\" · \"Clark County Treasurer · county-wide · 2026 tax year\" · official. The Tue 20 pickup row reads \"Recycling and garbage · Today\" in the done style (text.secondary), and cell 1 has no tonight outline. The week-two label above cell 8 reads \"Tue 27\".\n- Seeded civic rows take their mark from the rule's confidence. The voter and tax rows are drawn official only because this project assumes each seed was checked against its authority. An unchecked seed shows the hollow mark and the caption \"… · not yet checked against the source\".\n- Empty specimen (delta): a new account whose only saved place is \"Mom's place · Washougal, WA\", with no seeded pickup rule, viewed Mon 9 Nov 2026 (window Mon 9 Nov → Sun 22 Nov); chip \"Saved place · Only you\"; footer \"Only you will see this.\"\n- Phase-2 specimen (artboard 15 only, labelled \"Phase 2 (F10)\"), viewed Tue 20 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM (window Tue 20 Oct → Mon 2 Nov): \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18\" · \"in 3 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · you-added (tick); \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00\" · \"in 8 days · Wed 28 Oct\" · you-added (tick); \"Comcast · $79.99\" · \"in 13 days · Mon 2 Nov\" beside the narrowed county bar. The Tue 20 pickup row reads as in the county specimen. Summary \"Next 14 days: 8 items\". Beside the frame, a state column: overdue, \"Paid by Sam · 15 Oct\", \"A household bill is due\" (redacted for a viewer without bill access), and the amount \"$2,233.48\" right-aligned in tabular figures.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: The card is surface.base with radius lg and shadow sm. Top to bottom:\n1. Header: \"Next 14 days at this address\" in overline style, with the summary caption in text.secondary under it. One status line at a time sits under the summary (removed date, or saved outside the window), as a polite status, never a modal.\n2. Strip: 14 equal cells across the content width. On iOS that is about 23.5pt pitch, 2pt gaps and cells 56pt tall. \"Today\" sits above cell 1 and the week-two date (\"Mon 26\") above cell 8. A weekday initial sits beneath each cell. Each cell is surface.sunken with a 1.5px text.secondary baseline along its bottom edge; weekend cells use the same fill at 50% opacity, with the baseline and marks at full ink; the S S initials carry the meaning. The instrument skeleton has no baselines and no initials, so ready or empty cells never read as loading.\n3. Marks: each cell stacks up to 3 XS ProvenanceMarks (12pt) top-down in one ink, text.secondary. A cell draws one mark per pickup stream and one per other row, in row order, pickup streams first. \"+N\" in text.strong counts the marks not drawn; the summary counts rows. Shape is the only per-mark code. Kind is carried by the KindGlyph on the rows. Each kind uses its own KindGlyph from Foundations (including lease ends, notice deadline, insurance renews, warranty ends, HOA dues, property-tax), never a generic calendar icon. A combined pickup day has two marks and a garbage-only day has one.\n4. Region rule: a statewide or county rule is a full-height ink bar filling its cell (cell width minus 6pt, radius xs) with no mark inside. When that day also has address items, the bar narrows to 4pt at the cell's left edge and the marks sit to its right. Draw this narrowed form in context in artboard 15, and as a 4× cell callout beside artboard 05. The bar reads as \"a whole region\", never as a claim about this house.\n5. Tonight's pickup: the cell for tomorrow's pickup (cell 2 on Mon 19) gets a 1.5px text.primary outline, an emphasis, never a banner.\n6. Holiday move: the mark sits on the moved day. The usual day shows a struck ghost ring at 50% opacity. The row carries the caption.\n7. Pickup marks after the last published city calendar (Dec 2026) use the projected style. Record this on Notes only; it is outside every drawn window.\n8. Legend line under the strip, once, with S marks: \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\".\n9. DateRows in date order, each at least 56pt. Annual or self-entered rows (HOA dues, renters insurance, a pickup schedule the person set) get a 2px identity.home left rule plus their recurrence caption; seeded city pickup rows never get the rule. At a claimed home, a date the viewer kept private shows the ScopeChip person glyph plus \"Only you\" at the end of its SourceCaption line. A seeded pickup row whose frequency is Not set carries a visible 44pt text button \"Set your pickup day\" under its caption (first such row only; later rows offer it in their actions). The button opens the DateSheet in create mode with the Pickup day kind selected and Thursday prefilled. The same action appears in that row's custom actions and in its view-seeded DateSheet. The region chip on civic rows uses the DateRow region-chip slot: ScopeChip pill geometry with a map-region glyph (never the person or house glyph), spoken \"applies across Washington\" / \"applies across Clark County\", never \"Visible to …\". It is not a visibility chip.\n10. Foot row: \"+ Add a date\" (at least 44pt, primary.700), with the scope sentence under it.\nWhen data is missing: empty after a successful check shows drawn empty cells with their baselines, then \"Checked — nothing in the next 14 days\", then \"+ Add a date\". A failure draws no strip; an InlineErrorRow sits in the card. The card shows its own FreshnessLine only when the calendar is older than the rest of Today (\"Calendar updated 2h ago · Retry calendar\"). Otherwise the location row covers freshness.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: On native, cells are not targets. The whole strip is one adjustable element. iOS: swipe up or down to move a day, then double-tap to scroll to that day's first row and highlight it. Android TalkBack: the strip is one focusable node with a state description and the custom actions \"Next day\" / \"Previous day\". A plain tap on the strip scrolls to the rows. Web 1440: cells share the content width (about 47px each with 2px gaps, never under 44px), and only cells that hold items are buttons; each moves focus to its first row. The focus ring is a 2px border.focus ring with a 2px offset, distinct from the 1.5px tonight outline and from the highlight wash. Web 390: the strip is decorative and the rows carry everything. A row tap opens the DateSheet. Every row action is reachable without gestures: inside the DateSheet (Remind me, Mark done, Edit, and a \"Where this comes from\" row that swaps the sheet's content with a Back control, never stacking a second sheet). Screen readers also get them as custom actions: Edit, Remind me, Where this comes from, Mark done; seeded rows drop Edit, and an unset seeded pickup row adds \"Set your pickup day\". On web 1440 each row also has a 44px overflow button with the same actions. On a push or widget arrival, scroll once, fade in the DateRow highlighted wash in under 300ms, let it decay, and move focus to the row. Cells fill with a 150ms cross-fade when data lands. Under Reduce Motion: static highlight, no shimmer. Haptics: none here; the DateSheet save carries the one light tick.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: FourteenDayStrip (Today card; ready, empty, loading, stale, permission-denied, saved place, error, highlighted row), DateRow (pickup, deadline, holiday moved, money row in artboard 15 only; states default, highlighted, done, permission-hidden, unchecked seed, reported · checking, private at a home), KindGlyph (row 24pt), ProvenanceMark (XS in cells, S in rows and legend; reported variant), SourceCaption (short form), ScopeChip (footer sentence form; person glyph + \"Only you\" on a private row; the civic region chip is the DateRow slot above), QuietDayReceipt (strip empty, with the string below), WarmingSkeleton (instrument skeleton), InlineErrorRow, FreshnessLine (stale, offline), OfflineNotice, LockedActionRow (names who can act), DateSheet (create, view-mine, view-seeded), ProvenanceSheet.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: header, summary, status line, strip, legend, rows, add row. Strip label: \"Next 14 days: 4 items. Next: Recycling and garbage, tomorrow.\" Days are spoken as \"Tuesday 20 October: Recycling and garbage, your household's schedule, you added this\", \"Thursday 22 October: Pickup day, City of Camas schedule, on record, not confirmed\" or \"Friday 23 October: nothing\". Initials are never spoken. Each row is one element, e.g. \"Register or update to vote, online or mail, must arrive by Monday 26 October, in 7 days, applies across Washington, Washington Secretary of State, official\", \"Pay property tax, 2nd half, due Monday 2 November, in 13 days, applies across Clark County, Clark County Treasurer, official\" and \"HOA dues, 285 dollars, Sunday 1 November, in 13 days, added by Sam\". The \"Set your pickup day\" button is its own 44pt target after its row. The status lines use role=status. Marks are at least 12pt with a 1.5px stroke and 3:1 contrast in light and dark; the cell baseline is at least 3:1 against base. Rows wrap and never truncate. AX proposal: at AX3 and above, the cells give way to the summary sentence and the rows become the table; f1's AX5 frame uses the same fallback. Greyscale: every distinction is shape, count, bar, baseline or outline.\n\nCOPY: \"Next 14 days at this address\" · \"Next 14 days: 4 items\" · \"Today\" · \"Tomorrow\" · \"Tonight\" · \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct\" · \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\" · \"+ Add a date\" · \"Set your pickup day\" (delta) · \"Only you will see this.\" (saved place) · \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" (home) · \"Only you\" (private row at a home) · \"Statewide — WA\" · \"Clark County\" · \"Register or update to vote: online or mail\" · \"must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · \"In person: until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov\" · \"Pay property tax, 2nd half\" · \"For property owners in Clark County · moved from Sat 31 Oct\" · \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\" · \"You reported this · checking\" · \"not yet checked against the source\" · \"Sam added this · 3 Oct\" · \"You marked this done\" · \"Checked — nothing in the next 14 days\" (use this here even if the Foundations board shows \"two weeks\"; the research brief uses 14 days) · \"Saved · Lease ends Wed 31 Mar 2027 is in your place file · See it\" (delta) · \"That date was removed.\" · \"We couldn't load your calendar just now\" (delta) · \"Retry calendar\" · \"Calendar updated 2h ago · Retry calendar\" (delta) · \"You're offline · as of 4:10 PM\" · \"Adding a date needs a connection.\" (delta) · \"Maya can add dates here.\" (delta) · \"Pickup day\" · \"Which bins go out isn't set yet\" (delta) · \"City of Camas · weekday only · 2026 calendar\" (delta) · \"Repeats monthly\" (delta) · \"Repeats yearly\" (delta).\n\nEDGE CASES: Long titles wrap to two lines beside the glyph. Many items: more than 3 marks on one day show \"+N\" in the cell, and every item still gets a row. Zero items: the empty specimen. A date saved beyond the window: the place-file status line, never a silent toast. Slow network: the instrument skeleton reserves the final height and holds no text. Offline: the cached strip, the location row's \"You're offline · as of 4:10 PM\", and \"+ Add a date\" and \"Set your pickup day\" disabled with their reason. Permissions: by default a member such as Sam can add dates. A member whose calendar editing the owner turned off (or a Guest) sees rows but no add row, and a LockedActionRow names who can act. A viewer without bill access sees phase-2 money rows redacted. A saved place shows \"Only you will see this.\" and never uses household words. At a home, the add-row sentence states the DateSheet's default (\"Everyone in this household will see this.\"); the DateSheet lets the person keep a date to \"Only you\", and such rows show the private caption (f1 artboard 13 draws it). The voter row never states or implies registration status. Its \"Mark done\" is person-scoped (\"You marked this done\", Only you), and the household never sees it. The tax appeal never shows as a single seeded date; it is a conditional rule in the DateSheet and the place file. Camas has no Saturday bulk pickup.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of four class-coloured dots, draw one-ink marks told apart by shape — because hue alone fails greyscale and 3:1.\n- Instead of 14 tappable cells on phones, make the strip one element and the rows the targets — because 23pt cells are below 44pt and 48dp.\n- Instead of a dot, or a ScopeChip with a house glyph, for the voter deadline, draw a full-height bar and a region chip with a map glyph — because either would read as a claim about this house.\n- Instead of \"in 11 days\" alone, write \"in 11 days · Fri 30 Oct\" — because people act on deadlines by the date.\n- Instead of an even Thursday rhythm through Thanksgiving week, draw the moved mark and a struck ghost — because the usual day is wrong that week.\n- Instead of an empty strip when loading fails, draw no strip and a named Retry — because drawn empty cells with baselines mean \"checked, nothing found\".\n- Instead of a toast that vanishes after saving a far-off date, show the \"is in your place file · See it\" status line — because a saved date must never disappear from view.\n- Instead of a seeded pickup row that only opens a locked sheet, draw the \"Set your pickup day\" button in the row — because the first-week step needs a visible path.\n- Instead of a \"+ Date\" header toggle, keep \"+ Add a date\" as the last row — because a list gets a list row, not a mode switch.\n\nDONE WHEN: The hollow and tick marks are told apart in the cells at 1x in greyscale and dark (artboards 20 and 22), and the filled and tick marks in artboard 02. All three shapes are told apart in the rows and the legend. The Mon 26 bar cannot be read as a household fact. Empty, loading and error look clearly different; artboards 07 and 08 differ by baselines, initials and the receipt line even with the text covered. Every row beyond tomorrow shows its relative count, weekday and date, and every relative count matches its artboard's viewing date. Maya's confirmed Tuesdays show ticks, and combined days differ from garbage-only days. The PLACE B frame shows the hollow city weekday, the \"Set your pickup day\" button and an \"Only you\" footer. A reminder arrival lands on the exact row with focus. A date saved outside the window is still visibly findable. No phase-1 artboard shows a bill. No row is compressed below 56pt.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 01-ready-dense · light — HOME A, 4 items, tonight outline on cell 2, statewide bar, Sam's HOA row, inside Today.\n2. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 02-many-items · light — 6 items, \"+1\" on Tue 20 with filled and tick marks, wrapped insurance title.\n3. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 03-saved-place-unconfirmed · light — PLACE B, hollow Thursdays, \"Set your pickup day\" button on the Thu 22 row, Jordan's tick on Fri 30, \"Only you will see this.\"\n4. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 04-holiday-move · light — PLACE B on Mon 23 Nov, moved mark and struck ghost, Thu 3 Dec row \"You reported this · checking\".\n5. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 05-county-bar · light — HOME A on Tue 20 Oct at 6:10 PM, 5 items, done-style Tue 20 pickup row, full county bar on Mon 2 Nov; beside it the unchecked-seed row state and the 4× narrowed-bar callout.\n6. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 06-reminder-landing · light — the voter row highlighted and focused after its 7-day reminder, just before the DateSheet opens.\n7. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 07-empty-checked · light — Mom's place (new account, Mon 9 Nov): drawn empty cells with baselines, receipt line, add row, \"Only you will see this.\"\n8. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 08-loading · light — instrument skeleton, no baselines or initials.\n9. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 09-error-no-strip · light — InlineErrorRow, no strip.\n10. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 10-stale-partial · light — cached strip and rows, \"Calendar updated 2h ago · Retry calendar\".\n11. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 11-offline · light — cached strip and rows, \"You're offline · as of 4:10 PM\" in the location row, \"+ Add a date\" disabled with \"Adding a date needs a connection.\"\n12. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 12-edit-off-member · light — Sam's view after Maya turned off his calendar editing: rows only, LockedActionRow \"Maya can add dates here.\"\n13. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 13-removed-date-landing · light — \"That date was removed.\" under the summary as a polite status line, no modal.\n14. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 14-saved-outside-window · light — PLACE B after Jordan saves his lease end: \"Saved · Lease ends Wed 31 Mar 2027 is in your place file · See it\" under the summary, no new row.\n15. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 15-phase2-money-rows · light — labelled \"Phase 2 (F10)\", viewed Tue 20 Oct: 8 items, bill rows with ticks, the narrowed bar beside Comcast, and the state column.\n16. f5-today-calendar-strip · web-1440 · 01-ready-dense · light — about 47px cells, only filled cells focusable, focus ring shown on Tue 20, row overflow buttons.\n17. f5-today-calendar-strip · web-390 · 01-ready-dense · light — decorative strip.\n18. f5-today-calendar-strip · android · 01-ready-dense · light — 56dp rows, 48dp targets.\n19. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 16-ax5-proposal · light — AX5: summary sentence in place of the cells, wrapped rows (a proposal).\n20. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 17-greyscale · light — artboard 03 in greyscale at 1x.\n21. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 01-ready-dense · dark — dark twin of artboard 01.\n22. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 03-saved-place-unconfirmed · dark — dark twin of artboard 03 at 1x, proving hollow and tick read apart and the cell baselines hold 3:1.\n23. f5-today-calendar-strip · notes — every invented string and delta: Sam entering the HOA dues, the bulk pickup row, both renters-insurance rows and \"Repeats yearly\", the new-account \"Mom's place\" empty specimen, the PLACE B row copy, \"Set your pickup day\", Jordan's lease save and its status line, the report on Thu 3 Dec, the checked status of both civic seeds, the phase-2 bill states. Record the projected-style rule, the AX3 proposal and each artboard's viewing date and window. Record why the voter title reads \"Register or update to vote\": it names the action without implying registration status. Record contract clarifications for prompt 00: (1) the civic region-chip slot; (2) a housemate's entry uses the tick shape with \"<name> added this\"; (3) the strip-empty wording \"14 days\" replaces \"two weeks\" on the Foundations board; (4) a region bar shares a cell with address marks by narrowing to 4pt at the left edge; (5) DateRow gains the states \"unchecked seed\" (hollow mark + \"· not yet checked against the source\"), \"reported · checking\" (ProvenanceMark reported variant StatusLine) and \"private at a home\" (ScopeChip person glyph + \"Only you\" at the end of the SourceCaption); (6) strip cells are surface.sunken with a 1.5px text.secondary baseline, weekends at 50% fill; (7) an unset seeded pickup row carries a \"Set your pickup day\" button. Open question: whether the 2px left rule on a saved place should use identity.home green or text.secondary ink. List any omitted state.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1–6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7–12, then wait. Turn 3: 13–18, then wait. Turn 4: 19–23.",
