                    "issue": "Frame 9 asks for incompatible flood states in one frame: an unmapped flood zone and a Zone AE reading. The optional probability array is an open choice that will vary between turns.",
                    "evidence": "Artboard 9: \"what-if frame: flood not mapped, wildfire non-burnable, and the Zone AE reading line.\" LAYOUT: \"Optional: if you draw a picture for a 1%-a-year flood zone, draw a 4-cell or 100-cell array\".",
                    "fix": "Artboard 9 becomes 'three labelled crops: (a) flood \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\"; (b) wildfire \"Non-burnable land cover (USFS)\"; (c) flood \"Zone AE — 1% chance of flooding each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\" with its marker in band 3'. Delete the 'Optional' array sentence, or make it definite: 'In crop (c) only, under the row, draw a 100-cell array with 1 cell filled, captioned \"1 in 100 homes in this zone each year\"', and list that caption as invented."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Scope is not stated for single-home viewers. The named-home chip is drawn only for people with more than one home, and the prompt never says the page keeps its existing 'Your household' ScopeChip, which the contract requires on every surface showing address data.",
                    "evidence": "\"For people with more than one home only: the ScopeChip named-home variant\". Contract ScopeChip: \"It appears on every surface that shows address data.\"",
                    "fix": "Add to TYPE: 'Keep the screenshot's existing \"Your household\" ScopeChip in the page header on both pages. In frame 12 only, the block adds the named-home chip \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\".'"
