                "id": "f3-member-home-dashboard",
                "pass": false,
                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt makes every LockedActionRow open the verify sheet. That is wrong for the rows that name who can act ('Maya can add bills and mark them paid', 'Maya Chen can invite people here.', 'Maya can manage documents and security here'). Address verification does not grant members.manage, finance.manage or document management, so sending Sam to the verify sheet from those rows implies a path to rights he cannot get. It also contradicts the rule that no 'Request access' flow exists.",
                    "evidence": "Prompt: 'Tapping a LockedActionRow or its \"Verify address\" opens the verify sheet with that reason, which offers \"Ask Maya Chen to confirm\".' Design doc F3b: address verification unlocks 'residency letters, Residency Pass…, neighbor messages…' only. ux-research-brief.md: 'The prompts instead name who can mark a bill paid.' Prompt INSTEAD OF: 'Instead of a \"Request access\" flow, draw only the owner's name'.",
                    "fix": "Split the rule: 'Tapping a verification LockedActionRow (residency letter, neighbor messages) or its \"Verify address\" opens the verify sheet with that reason. Rows that name who can act are informational; their only target is the trailing \"View\".'"
                  },
