        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f3-bill-detail-web",
            "name": "Bill detail (new web route)",
            "platforms": [
              "web"
            ],
            "isNew": true,
            "frameCount": 27,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Bill detail · f3-bill-detail-web\n\nTYPE: NEW. Web only. Web has no page for a single bill today, so every money notification lands on a list. Match the attached Bills list and native bill detail. Use no new card style.\n\nATTACH: the web Bills list at 1440 and 390; the web Place tab with the left sidebar at 1440; the iOS bill detail screen (for content order only).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 with the left sidebar (Place selected); web 390x844 with the four-tab bottom bar (Place selected). Draw no native frames; iOS and Android keep their own bill detail.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab › Larkspur Loop › Bills › one bill. URL /app/homes/{home}/bills/{bill}. Arrivals:\n1. A single \"marked paid\" row in Notifications (/app/notifications). The page opens in the Paid state. A grouped \"Maya marked 3 bills paid\" row lands on the Bills list instead (/app/homes/{home}/bills?segment=paid&highlight={bill1},{bill2},{bill3}).\n2. A bill reminder row, sent the day before and the day of.\n3. A Bills list row (the whole row is the link). Back returns to the list, restores its scroll position and puts focus on that row, with no wash.\n4. The Today 14-day strip money row (phase 2).\n5. \"Added to bills\" on a Mail piece (phase 2).\nWeb gets no push. A phone push opens the native bill detail, and the in-app row is the web twin. A notification row for a bill that has since been removed opens this URL and shows this page's removed state (frame 17); browser Back returns to Notifications. What happens next: Mark paid → Undo stays open → Maya leaves the page → Sam gets one \"marked paid\" notification → Sam taps it and lands here in the Paid state.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, at her laptop on Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM. She just paid Clark Public Utilities on the utility's website and opened the bill from its row in Bills, so Sam doesn't pay it too. Maya is the only person at HOME A who can mark bills paid. Second viewer: Sam Ortega, a member who can see bills but cannot mark them paid. He opens the same bill from \"Maya marked Clark Public Utilities paid\". Jenna, a guest until Tue 20 Oct, cannot see bills.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Give every bill notification, reminder and calendar row one exact page that shows the amount, the due date and who marked it paid.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first the amount \"$142.18\" (h1, tabular figures); second the due line \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" (h3, text.secondary) with one StatusChip \"Upcoming\" at its end; third the single primary button \"Mark paid\". Everything else sits below these as evidence.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas)\n- Bill: Clark Public Utilities · Electric · account ending 4417 · $142.18 · due Fri 23 Oct · repeats monthly · ScopeChip \"Your household\" with the caption \"Maya and Sam can see this bill\" · Details \"Visible to: Maya and Sam\" · Added by Maya · Sat 3 Oct · Reminders: Thu 22 Oct · Fri 23 Oct (day before and day of). After marking: \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" and Details \"Reminders: Sun 22 Nov · Mon 23 Nov\".\n- Visibility rule: \"Visible to: Your household\" (and no caption) only when everyone at the home can see bills. While anyone cannot (today, Jenna), name the people.\n- Overdue: NW Natural · Gas · $41.18 · \"Overdue · was due Tue 13 Oct, 6 days ago\".\n- Only-you bill: State Farm renters insurance · $22.50 · \"Due in 19 days · Sat 7 Nov\".\n- Former member: City of Vancouver water, August bill, $81.60, added by hand, \"Marked paid by Theo (no longer here) · Fri 28 Aug\". Its trend: May to Aug 2026 only (78.40, 80.10, 88.25, 81.60).\n- Phase 2 only (frame 03 and its inset), owned by the f10-bill-provenance and f10-bill-trend projects. Provenance for Maya: \"From a photo you took · Sat 3 Oct\" with a 56pt thumbnail, \"We read this from your photo. You confirmed the amount on Sat 3 Oct.\", \"View the photo\", \"Fix what we read\". For any other viewer: \"From a photo Maya took · Sat 3 Oct\" and \"We read this from Maya's photo. Maya confirmed the amount on Sat 3 Oct.\" Trend, using the f10-bill-trend board's values: \"Clark PUD — last 12 months\", Nov 2025 to Oct 2026: 118.22, 167.05, 198.73, 186.41, 151.60, 112.88, 94.15, 88.02, 103.77, 121.34, 109.60, 142.18. Nearby average $127.40 from 14 homes. Caption for Maya: \"Your amounts. The line is the average of 14 homes nearby.\" For Sam: \"Your household's amounts. The line is the average of 14 homes nearby.\"\n- Worst case: provider \"City of Vancouver Water, Sewer and Stormwater Utility\"; amount $3,412.56 on \"Clark County Treasurer · Property tax, 2nd half\", due Mon 2 Nov, with the detail line \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Heading: the semantic h1 is \"Clark Public Utilities, $142.18\". Inside that one heading, the provider is styled h2 and the amount is styled h1.\n- StatusChip placement, on every frame: the chip sits at the end of the due line. At 390 it wraps under the due line.\n- 1440: breadcrumb \"Place › Larkspur Loop › Bills › Clark Public Utilities\", then a 2/3 + 1/3 split. Left column, top to bottom: provider with ScopeChip \"Your household\" and its caption \"Maya and Sam can see this bill\"; amount; due line with the StatusChip; attribution line (Paid only); action row with the primary \"Mark paid\" (primary.700 fill), the text buttons \"Paid a different amount\" and \"Skip this month\", and an overflow menu button holding \"Edit\" and \"Remove\". Right column: a \"Details\" card with label/value rows: Type, Account, Repeats, Visible to, Added by, Reminders.\n- Only-you bill: drop the ScopeChip and its caption and print the sentence \"Only you will see this.\" under the provider. Details reads \"Visible to: Only you\".\n- 390: one column: a \"Bills\" back link, provider, ScopeChip and caption, amount, due line, chip wrapped under it, a full-width \"Mark paid\", the secondary actions stacked, then Details.\n- Loop phase (every frame except 03): no provenance block and no trend, and no empty slot for either.\n- Phase 2 (frame 03 only): the provenance block, then the trend, beneath the left column's action row (on 390, beneath Details). Trend: the bill-trend card exactly as the f10-bill-trend board draws it: 12 zero-based columns, the current month labelled \"$142\" and carrying a ProvenanceMark S tick, one reference line labelled \"Nearby average $127 · 14 homes\", the summary sentence \"October: $142.18. Nearby average: $127, from 14 homes.\" above it, and a \"Show amounts\" list of all 12 values below. Fallbacks: too few homes → columns, no line, caption \"Not enough homes nearby to compare yet\"; partial history → empty labelled month slots, never $0; cold load → WarmingSkeleton instrument variant; failure → InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't load the last 12 months\" + \"Retry\", with the bill above still live.\n- A bill added by hand has no provenance block and no empty slot for one.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Mark paid: the button row becomes the InlineUndo line \"Marked paid · Undo\" (role=status). The chip changes to \"Paid\". The attribution reads \"Marked paid by you · Mon 19 Oct\". \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" appears. Under it: \"No more reminders for October's bill, for anyone.\" Details Reminders changes to \"Sun 22 Nov · Mon 23 Nov\". A caption reads \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this page.\" The paid status is saved at once, so Sam's list and bill detail show \"Marked paid by Maya\" straight away. Only the \"marked paid\" notification waits for Maya to leave the page; if she closes the tab, it is sent then. Undo stays until she leaves, restores everything and sends nothing. Leaving sends exactly one \"marked paid\" notification to each other person who can see bills (today, only Sam). Marking paid also cancels October's scheduled reminders for every member and replaces any reminder already delivered with the \"marked paid\" notification. November's reminders stay.\n- Overdue bill: the primary still reads \"Mark paid\" and behaves exactly as above.\n- Paid a different amount: an inline amount field pre-filled with $142.18, a button that restates the value (\"Mark $120.00 paid\") and a \"Cancel\" text button beside it. Cancel or Escape closes the field and changes nothing. After committing, the amount reads \"$120.00\" with the caption \"Bill was $142.18\" under it, the attribution reads \"Marked paid by you · Mon 19 Oct\", and InlineUndo reads \"Marked $120.00 paid · Undo\". Next due, the reminders line and the notice caption behave as for Mark paid.\n- Skip this month: skips only October. InlineUndo \"Skipped this month · Undo\" plus \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\". It cancels this month's reminders and sends no household notice.\n- Edit opens the existing bill edit form for this bill; its design is out of scope.\n- Remove: no dialog. The page collapses to \"Removed Clark Public Utilities · Undo\" with the caption \"This removes the monthly bill and its future months.\", then \"Sam won't see it anymore.\" and \"Back to bills\". For a bill made from a photo, the line reads \"Removed Clark Public Utilities and its photo · Undo\" (the InlineUndo bill + photo variant, owned by f10-bill-provenance). A removed bill also leaves the Bills list's Upcoming segment.\n- Race: a second Mark paid on a bill already marked paid shows \"Already marked paid by you on your phone · 6:02 PM\" with the Paid chip, and nothing is sent twice. When a different person who can mark bills paid got there first, the line names them (\"Already marked paid by <name> · 6:02 PM\"). HOME A has no second such person, so draw only the phone case.\n- Deep-link arrival: focus moves to the h1 and the headline block fades a highlight once (300ms). With Reduce Motion, show the highlight without the fade. Escape closes the overflow menu. Web has no haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: StatusChip (Upcoming · Due today · Overdue with the error glyph · Paid); ScopeChip (\"Your household\"; sentence form \"Only you will see this.\"); InlineUndo (marked paid, different amount, skipped, removed, bill + photo deleted); LockedActionRow (\"names who can act\" variant); ProvenanceMark and SourceCaption (phase-2 block and trend); WarmingSkeleton; InlineErrorRow; FreshnessLine; OfflineNotice; BillRow (only on the list you return to).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: breadcrumb, heading (provider and amount), scope chip and caption, due line and status, attribution, primary action, Details, then phase-2 evidence and trend. Document title \"Clark Public Utilities bill, $142.18\". The chart is role=img labelled with its summary sentence, followed by the \"Show amounts\" list. The tick keeps its fixed spoken name \"you added this\"; the person goes in the row label, e.g. \"October, 142 dollars 18 cents, added by Maya, you added this\". Targets are 44px. \"Overdue\" is a word plus a glyph, never colour alone. The Oct column is labelled and outlined in primary.800, not only filled. Undo announces politely and is focusable. A disabled control keeps focus and reads its reason. At 200% browser zoom on 1440 (720 CSS px) the Details column drops below the main column.\n\nCOPY: \"Mark paid\" · \"Paid a different amount\" · \"Mark $120.00 paid\" · \"Cancel\" · \"Skip this month\" · \"Edit\" · \"Remove\" · \"Marked paid · Undo\" · \"Marked $120.00 paid · Undo\" · \"Bill was $142.18\" · \"Skipped this month · Undo\" · \"Removed Clark Public Utilities · Undo\" · \"This removes the monthly bill and its future months.\" · \"Removed Clark Public Utilities and its photo · Undo\" · \"Sam won't see it anymore.\" · \"Back to bills\" · \"Marked paid by you · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Marked paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Marked paid by Theo (no longer here) · Fri 28 Aug\" · \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" · \"No more reminders for October's bill, for anyone.\" · \"Reminders: Thu 22 Oct · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"Reminders: Sun 22 Nov · Mon 23 Nov\" · \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"Due today\" · \"Overdue · was due Tue 13 Oct, 6 days ago\" · \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this page.\" · \"Maya can mark this paid.\" · \"Already marked paid by you on your phone · 6:02 PM\" · \"Maya and Sam can see this bill\" · \"Visible to: Maya and Sam\" / \"Visible to: Your household\" / \"Visible to: Only you\" · \"Only you will see this.\" · \"That bill was removed.\" + \"Back to bills\" · \"You can't see this bill\" / \"Bills at Larkspur Loop are shared with Maya and Sam. Maya can change your access.\" + \"Back to Larkspur Loop\" · \"We couldn't load this bill. Check your connection, then try again.\" + \"Retry\" · \"You're offline · as of 5:40 PM\" · \"Marking paid needs a connection.\" · \"Not enough homes nearby to compare yet\" · \"We couldn't load the last 12 months\" · \"Show amounts\".\n\nEDGE CASES: Wrap the longest provider name to two lines; the amount never truncates, and $3,412.56 fits the amount line at 390. The attribution line wraps and never truncates before the name (\"Marked paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\"). A Paid landing is reassurance, not an error: neutral chip, no error or success slab; it occurs only after a \"marked paid\" notification or in a race. No reminder for a paid month can reach anyone. A member (Sam) sees no Mark paid, Skip, Edit or Remove, only LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark this paid.\" An Only-you bill never sends a \"marked paid\" notification and shows no \"We'll let Sam know\" caption. A guest without bill access sees the denied page with no provider or amount. A removed bill opened from a stale notification shows \"That bill was removed.\" Offline keeps the cached values and disables the actions, each with its reason. Due today is drawn as if viewed on Fri 23 Oct.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of putting the provenance block or the trend above the amount, draw them beneath it, because they are evidence for the number the reader came to see.\n- Instead of paired bars or a second peer series, draw one reference line with its count of homes, because paired bars suggest one household competing with another.\n- Instead of a confidence percentage on the read, draw the sentence \"You confirmed the amount on Sat 3 Oct\", because a percentage makes people distrust a value they already checked.\n- Instead of a confirm dialog for Mark paid, draw the InlineUndo line and hold the household notice until Maya leaves, because undo prevents mis-taps without adding a step.\n- Instead of a second label such as \"Already paid\" on an overdue bill, keep \"Mark paid\", because one job gets one button name.\n- Instead of a greyed Mark paid for a member, draw LockedActionRow naming Maya, because Sam needs to know who can record it.\n- Instead of \"Reminders are off for this bill\" on a repeating bill, say October's reminders stopped and list November's dates, because the series continues.\n- Instead of a 404 or blank page for a removed bill, draw \"That bill was removed.\" with Back to bills, because a stale notification must never dead-end.\n\nDONE WHEN: Within five seconds, Maya can say what she owes, when it is due and what to press. After she presses Mark paid, the page says Sam will be told, and he is told only once, when she leaves. Sam lands on a calm, loop-phase Paid page naming Maya, with no provenance or trend. No October reminder can reach Sam after the bill is paid, and November's reminder dates are visible. The visibility line is true on every frame. Every arrival resolves to this bill or to a designed fallback, never a list or a blank page.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 01-upcoming-dense · light — Maya's loop-phase view: Clark $142.18, due line \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" ending in the Upcoming chip, ScopeChip with \"Maya and Sam can see this bill\", Mark paid row, Details card with \"Visible to: Maya and Sam\"; no provenance block, no trend, no empty slots.\n2. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 02-marked-paid-undo · light — \"Marked paid · Undo\", Paid chip, \"Marked paid by you · Mon 19 Oct\", \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\", \"No more reminders for October's bill, for anyone.\", Details \"Reminders: Sun 22 Nov · Mon 23 Nov\", notice caption.\n3. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 03-phase2-evidence · light — frame 01 plus \"From a photo you took · Sat 3 Oct\" and the 12-month trend beneath the actions; plus a 520-wide inset labelled \"Other viewer\" showing Sam's provenance line \"From a photo Maya took · Sat 3 Oct\", its sentence, and the household trend caption.\n4. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 04-paid-landing-member · light — loop phase: Sam from the notification, focus on the h1 with the one-time highlight, Paid chip, \"Marked paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\", \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\", no action row, no provenance, no trend.\n5. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 05-member-unpaid · light — Sam, Upcoming, LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark this paid.\"\n6. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 06-due-today · light — viewed Fri 23 Oct, arrived from the day-of reminder row, chip \"Due today\".\n7. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 07-overdue · light — NW Natural $41.18, StatusChip Overdue with its error glyph at the end of \"Overdue · was due Tue 13 Oct, 6 days ago\", primary \"Mark paid\".\n8. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 08-only-you-bill · light — State Farm renters insurance $22.50, \"Only you will see this.\", no ScopeChip, \"Visible to: Only you\"; an inset after Mark paid with no \"We'll let Sam know\" caption.\n9. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 09-upcoming · light — one-column version of 01, chip wrapped under the due line.\n10. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 10-marked-paid-undo · light — one-column version of 02.\n11. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 11-paid-different-amount · light — inline amount field showing $120.00, \"Mark $120.00 paid\" and \"Cancel\".\n12. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 12-different-amount-committed · light — \"$120.00\", \"Bill was $142.18\", \"Marked $120.00 paid · Undo\".\n13. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 13-manual-bill-insufficient-peers · light — August water bill $81.60, \"Marked paid by Theo (no longer here) · Fri 28 Aug\", no provenance block; phase-2 trend with May–Aug columns, no line, \"Not enough homes nearby to compare yet\".\n14. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 14-mark-paid-race · light — \"Already marked paid by you on your phone · 6:02 PM\", Paid chip, nothing re-sent.\n15. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 15-skipped-this-month · light — \"Skipped this month · Undo\", \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\", no notice caption.\n16. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 16-removed-undo · light — page collapsed to \"Removed Clark Public Utilities · Undo\", \"This removes the monthly bill and its future months.\", \"Sam won't see it anymore.\", Back to bills.\n17. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 17-removed-arrival · light — arrived from a stale notification: \"That bill was removed.\" and Back to bills.\n18. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 18-permission-denied · light — Jenna's guest view, no amount or provider, \"Bills at Larkspur Loop are shared with Maya and Sam. Maya can change your access.\"\n19. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 19-loading · light — WarmingSkeleton in final geometry.\n20. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 20-error · light — load failed with Retry.\n21. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 21-offline · light — cached values, \"You're offline · as of 5:40 PM\", disabled actions with \"Marking paid needs a connection.\"\n22. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 22-worst-case · light — longest provider on two lines and $3,412.56 property tax with \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n23. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 23-200-percent · light — 200% browser zoom (720 CSS px): Details card below the main column, amount and actions wrap, nothing truncates.\n24. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 24-greyscale · light — frame 01 in greyscale.\n25. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 01-upcoming-dense · dark — dark twin of 1.\n26. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 02-marked-paid-undo · dark — dark twin of 2 (InlineUndo line, Paid chip, notice caption on dark surfaces).\n27. f3-bill-detail-web · Notes — assumptions (Maya's arrival from the Bills row; the reminder-row arrival drawn only on Fri 23 Oct; Skip affects one month and Remove affects the series; Only-you bills never notify; due today viewed on Fri 23 Oct; the inventory's \"Already paid\" folded into \"Mark paid\"; trend values taken from the f10-bill-trend board; the trend error string aligned to that board; detail uses the longer \"Marked paid by\" on purpose, per the \"marked paid\" glossary rule, while Bills list rows keep the BillRow string \"Paid by Maya\"; the visibility line names Maya and Sam while Jenna's guest access lasts and switches to \"Your household\" after Tue 20 Oct; the race pattern \"Already marked paid by <name> · 6:02 PM\" for a future second person who can mark bills paid, not drawn because HOME A has none; open question: the tick's spoken name for other viewers is drawn as the fixed \"you added this\" with \"added by Maya\" in the row label, and the Foundations legend overrides this if the two disagree); every invented string (account 4417, NW Natural, State Farm, Theo, the August water amounts, $120.00, 6:02 PM, the Sun 22 Nov and Mon 23 Nov reminder dates, \"Maya and Sam can see this bill\", \"This removes the monthly bill and its future months.\", the other-viewer provenance and trend captions); omitted states owned elsewhere (photo deleted but bill kept, low-confidence caution, View the mail — f10-bill-provenance; the bill edit form); and the open product decision on letting members record \"I paid this\".\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue. Turn 5: 25-27.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Removed the impossible 'Already marked paid by Sam' race string from INTERACTION and COPY; kept only the phone case and added the '<name>' pattern for a future second manager to Notes (review major).",
              "Visibility now true: ScopeChip 'Your household' plus caption 'Maya and Sam can see this bill', Details 'Visible to: Maya and Sam', with the rule that 'Your household' is used only when everyone can see bills; updated COPY and frames 1 and 18 (review major + minor).",
              "Replaced the misleading 'Reminders are off for this bill, for everyone' with 'No more reminders for October's bill, for anyone.' and Details 'Reminders: Sun 22 Nov · Mon 23 Nov' (P18 whole series); added matching INSTEAD OF line (review major).",
              "Frame 04 is now the loop-phase Paid landing for Sam (no provenance, no trend); Sam's phase-2 captions moved to a 520-wide 'Other viewer' inset in frame 03 (review major).",
              "Added dark twin 26 of frame 02; Notes renumbered to 27; Turn 5 now 25-27 (review major).",
              "Fixed one StatusChip placement everywhere: at the end of the due line, wrapping under it at 390 (review minor).",
              "Added a Cancel text button (and Escape) to 'Paid a different amount'; stated that Edit opens the existing bill edit form, out of scope (review minor).",
              "Remove now carries the caption 'This removes the monthly bill and its future months.'; Skip is stated as one month only (review minor).",
              "Tick keeps the contract's fixed spoken name 'you added this' with the person in the row label; the open question stays on Notes with the Foundations legend overriding (review minor x2).",
              "Denied copy no longer uses 'members': 'Bills at Larkspur Loop are shared with Maya and Sam. Maya can change your access.'; replaced internal 'bill_paid' with 'the \"marked paid\" notification' in instructions (review minor).",
              "Notes records that detail uses 'Marked paid by' on purpose while BillRow keeps 'Paid by' (review minor).",
              "Stated that a stale notification for a removed bill opens this page's removed state, with browser Back returning to Notifications, to align with f3-household-notifications (cross-prompt consistency)."
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f3-bills-list",
            "name": "Bills list (member read-only + payer attribution)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 26,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Bills list · f3-bills-list\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Bills list\" (and the dashboard Bills card it opens from). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: the Bills list on web 1440, web 390, iOS and Android; the home dashboard Bills card; the native bill detail on iOS and Android.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 (left sidebar) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar); iOS 393x852 (large title \"Bills\", back \"Larkspur Loop\"); Android 412x915 (Material 3 top app bar). Place is the selected tab everywhere.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab › Larkspur Loop (place file) › Money section › Bills. Other ways in:\n- the home dashboard Bills card \"View\";\n- the home header Bills tab;\n- a grouped \"marked paid\" notification (\"Maya marked 3 bills paid\"), from the push or from the \"See all 3 in Bills\" line under the expanded in-app row, which opens the Paid segment with those three rows highlighted: /app/homes/{home}/bills?segment=paid&highlight={bill1},{bill2},{bill3};\n- a single highlighted row: /app/homes/{home}/bills?linkedType=bill&linkedId={bill};\n- Back from bill detail, which restores the scroll position and returns focus to the row you came from, with no wash and no announcement.\nA single \"marked paid\" notification opens bill detail, not this list. Every row hands off to bill detail (web /app/homes/{home}/bills/{bill}; native pantopus://homes/{home}/bills/{bill}).\n\nWHO AND WHEN: The dense default is Sam Ortega's phone on Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM. Sam is a member at HOME A. He can see bills, but only Maya can mark them paid. He checks whether the power bill is handled before paying it himself. Jenna, a guest until Tue 20 Oct, cannot see bills. The manage frames are Maya Chen's (owner).\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let everyone in the household see the bills and who marked each one paid, so two people do not pay the same bill.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first the header: ScopeChip \"Your household\" with \"Maya and Sam can see these bills\" and \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov · 1 overdue ($41.18)\"; second the column of amounts; third each row's right-hand line: \"Not marked paid yet\" or \"Paid by Maya\". The primary action is opening a row. There is no mark-paid button on any row face.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas)\n- Upcoming (fixtures): Clark Public Utilities $142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct; City of Vancouver water $84.00 · due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct; Comcast $79.99 · due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov.\n- Overdue (delta): NW Natural $41.18 · was due Tue 13 Oct · Overdue. The header reads exactly \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov · 1 overdue ($41.18)\". The overdue amount stays out of the window total.\n- Paid (delta), newest first: Clark Public Utilities $109.60 (September bill, due Wed 23 Sep) · Paid by Maya · Thu 17 Sep; Comcast $79.99 (due Fri 2 Oct) · Paid by Maya · Thu 17 Sep; Waste Connections $38.75 (quarterly, due Wed 30 Sep) · Paid by Maya · Thu 17 Sep; City of Vancouver water $81.60 · Paid by Theo (no longer here) · Fri 28 Aug. The three Thu 17 Sep rows are the grouped notification's rows.\n- HOA dues ($285, Sun 1 Nov) are a date on the calendar, not a household bill, so they are not in this list or its totals.\n- Only-you bill (delta, Maya's view only): State Farm renters insurance $22.50 · due in 19 days · Sat 7 Nov.\n- Scope sentence rule: print \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills\" only when every person at the home can see bills. When anyone cannot (today, Jenna the guest), name the people: \"Maya and Sam can see these bills\".\n- Worst case: provider \"City of Vancouver Water, Sewer and Stormwater Utility\"; \"Clark County Treasurer · Property tax, 2nd half\" $3,412.56 due Mon 2 Nov; the header then reads \"4 upcoming · $3,718.73 through Mon 2 Nov · 1 overdue ($41.18)\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Header, in this order: ScopeChip; the scope sentence; the count and window total; a FreshnessLine; on Sam's view, LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark bills paid.\"; then the ChoiceChip segment Upcoming / Paid / All (iOS segmented control, Android M3 filter chips).\n- Rows use BillRow, identical on all three platforms. Line 1: provider (bodyMedium, truncates first), one StatusChip, and the amount right-aligned in tabular figures, so the amounts form one column. Line 2: the due date (bodySmall, text.secondary) and, right-aligned, the attribution slot. On paid rows the slot reads \"Paid by Maya · Thu 17 Sep\"; on Sam's unpaid rows it reads \"Not marked paid yet\" (bodySmall, text.secondary). The name never truncates. Paid rows use the Paid chip. Overdue rows use the Overdue chip with its glyph.\n- Member rows (Sam): the BillRow member variant is drawn as the header LockedActionRow plus each unpaid row's \"Not marked paid yet\"; no \"I paid this\" item is drawn.\n- Only-you bill: line 1 keeps its single StatusChip; line 2's right slot shows a 12pt person glyph plus the words \"Only you\" in bodySmall text.secondary, in the attribution position. Only-you bills are left out of the header count and total; Maya's header adds \"1 bill only you can see\".\n- Upcoming shows the overdue group first, under the overline \"OVERDUE\", then the upcoming rows. The All segment adds month overlines once there are more than 20 rows.\n- Manage (Maya): each row has an overflow button (44pt iOS / 48dp Android / 44px web) with \"Mark paid\", \"Paid a different amount\" and \"Skip this month\". Sam's rows have no overflow; the whole row opens detail.\n- Highlight from a notification: the target rows scroll into view once, get an infoBg wash plus a 2pt leading bar in primary.700 (a shape cue that survives greyscale), and the first receives accessibility focus. The wash fades over 300ms once the person scrolls. The highlight opens nothing by itself. Back from detail gets no highlight.\n- Draw no budget bar, spend meter or ring.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Mark paid (overflow): the row changes in place to InlineUndo \"Marked Clark Public Utilities paid · Undo\", with the caption \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this screen.\" under it (web: \"…when you leave this page.\"; no caption for Only-you bills). On Android it is echoed by a Snackbar with Undo that stays open while TalkBack is on. On iOS the inline line is also announced. Undo lasts until Maya leaves the screen and sends nothing. The paid status is saved at once; the household \"marked paid\" notification is sent only after she leaves, October's reminders stop for everyone, and the repeating bill reappears in Upcoming as \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\".\n- Paid a different amount (overflow): opens bill detail with the amount field focused.\n- Skip this month (overflow): the row collapses to \"Skipped this month · Undo\" plus \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\". It sends no household notice.\n- Race: if the bill was already marked paid on another device, the row reads \"Already marked paid by you on your phone · 6:02 PM\", and nothing is sent twice. HOME A has no second person who can mark bills paid, so draw only this case.\n- The overflow menu is also exposed as custom accessibility actions. There are no swipe-only actions.\n- Pull to refresh (native) refreshes in place with FreshnessLine \"Updating…\" and no full-screen spinner. Web has a Refresh text button in the FreshnessLine.\n- Haptics: one light tick when Maya taps Mark paid and the InlineUndo line appears (iOS light impact; Android CONFIRM). No haptic on Undo or on Skip.\n- Reduce Motion: the highlight appears and clears with no fade or scroll animation.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: BillRow (manage, member, only-me and former-member variants; highlighted and marked-paid states); StatusChip; ChoiceChip (segment); ScopeChip (\"Your household\"); LockedActionRow (\"names who can act\" variant); InlineUndo; FreshnessLine; OfflineNotice; WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton); InlineErrorRow.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: ScopeChip, scope sentence, count and total, FreshnessLine, lock row, segment, rows. Each row is one merged element, for example \"Clark Public Utilities, 142 dollars 18 cents, due Friday October 23, upcoming, not marked paid yet\", \"…, paid by Maya on Thursday September 17\" or \"State Farm renters insurance, 22 dollars 50 cents, due Saturday November 7, upcoming, only you can see this\". The overflow items are custom actions. A row highlighted from a notification gets focus and the announcement \"From your notification\". Overdue and Only you are words, not colour. The segment shows selection with a check plus fill, which differs from the focus ring. Targets are 44pt iOS, 48dp Android and 44px web. At AX5 and 200%, line 2 stacks under line 1, the amount moves under the provider, and the segment becomes radio rows. Undo announces as a status.\n\nCOPY: \"Maya and Sam can see these bills\" · \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills\" · \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov · 1 overdue ($41.18)\" · \"4 upcoming · $3,718.73 through Mon 2 Nov · 1 overdue ($41.18)\" · \"OVERDUE\" · \"Maya can mark bills paid.\" · \"Upcoming\" / \"Paid\" / \"All\" · \"Mark paid\" · \"Paid a different amount\" · \"Skip this month\" · \"Marked Clark Public Utilities paid · Undo\" · \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this screen.\" / \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this page.\" · \"Skipped this month · Undo\" · \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" · \"Not marked paid yet\" · \"Paid by Maya · Thu 17 Sep\" · \"Paid by you · Thu 17 Sep\" · \"Paid by Theo (no longer here) · Fri 28 Aug\" · \"Already marked paid by you on your phone · 6:02 PM\" · \"Only you\" · \"1 bill only you can see\" · \"Checked — no household bills on file\" + \"Add a bill\" (manage) / \"Maya can add bills here.\" (member) · \"Checked — nothing due. Paid bills are under Paid.\" · \"We couldn't load your bills just now\" + \"Retry\" · \"You're offline · as of 5:40 PM\" · \"Amounts and paid status as of 5:40 PM. Changes since then aren't shown.\" · \"Marking paid needs a connection.\" · \"Updated 2h ago\" · \"Updating…\" · \"Refresh\" · \"You can't see these bills\" / \"Bills at Larkspur Loop are shared with Maya and Sam. Maya can change your access.\" · \"From your notification\".\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest provider truncates before the amount or the attribution. $3,412.56 keeps the amount column aligned. With 20+ bills in All, use month overlines. Draw zero bills for both manage and member. Draw an empty Upcoming with a populated Paid. A removed bill never appears in Upcoming, and returning from a removed bill shows no highlighted row. On a slow network, a cold load uses the row skeleton; a warm load keeps the rows. Offline and stale states say what is stale. A guest without bill access (Jenna) gets the denied state with no providers or amounts. A saved place never reaches this list: its place file shows the Money section as not available for a saved place. Only-you bills appear only for their owner, never count toward the household total and never notify.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a one-tap Mark paid on the row face or the dashboard card, keep it in the overflow with InlineUndo, because a mis-tap would tell the whole household.\n- Instead of an avatar without a name, print \"Paid by Maya\", because the name is the point.\n- Instead of a greyed Mark paid for Sam, draw LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark bills paid.\", because he needs to know who can record it.\n- Instead of leaving an unpaid row's right slot blank for Sam, print \"Not marked paid yet\", because absence is not an answer.\n- Instead of a budget bar, spend meter or percentage ring, show the count and window total as text, because this list is about who paid, not a score.\n- Instead of a highlight that only changes colour, add the leading bar and move focus, because the wash is invisible in greyscale and to screen readers.\n- Instead of an \"Only you\" chip beside the StatusChip, put the person glyph and \"Only you\" in line 2's right slot, because one row has one chip.\n- Instead of \"Everyone\" when a guest can't see bills, name the people, because the scope line must be true.\n\nDONE WHEN: Sam can tell in five seconds that Clark Public Utilities is not yet marked paid and that only Maya can mark it. Maya can mark a bill paid and undo it without anyone being told, and she is told Sam will hear when she leaves. The grouped notification lands on the right three rows with focus. The header always states who can see the bills, the window total and the overdue amount separately, and every statement is true.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f3-bills-list · ios · 01-upcoming-member-dense · light — Sam's view: header with \"Maya and Sam can see these bills\", \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov · 1 overdue ($41.18)\", lock row, overdue group and three upcoming rows each reading \"Not marked paid yet\".\n2. f3-bills-list · web-1440 · 02-upcoming-manage · light — Maya's view with overflow buttons and \"1 bill only you can see\".\n3. f3-bills-list · android · 03-upcoming-manage · light — Maya's view.\n4. f3-bills-list · ios · 04-paid-segment · light — Sam's view, attribution on every row, including Theo.\n5. f3-bills-list · ios · 05-all-segment · light — Sam's view, mixed statuses.\n6. f3-bills-list · android · 06-overflow-open · light — Maya's view, the menu with the three actions.\n7. f3-bills-list · ios · 07-marked-paid-undo · light — Maya's view, \"Marked Clark Public Utilities paid · Undo\" in the row, \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this screen.\", plus Next due Mon 23 Nov.\n8. f3-bills-list · android · 08-marked-paid-snackbar · light — Maya's view, Snackbar held open with TalkBack on.\n9. f3-bills-list · ios · 09-skipped-this-month · light — Maya's view, \"Skipped this month · Undo\" and Next due Mon 23 Nov.\n10. f3-bills-list · web-390 · 10-highlighted-grouped · light — Sam's view, Paid segment with the three Thu 17 Sep rows highlighted (wash plus leading bar), focus on the first.\n11. f3-bills-list · ios · 11-back-focus-restored · light — Sam's view back from bill detail: scroll restored, focus ring on the Clark row, no wash.\n12. f3-bills-list · ios · 12-only-you-bill · light — Maya's list with the State Farm row showing the person glyph and \"Only you\" in line 2.\n13. f3-bills-list · web-1440 · 13-empty · light — manage and member empty states side by side.\n14. f3-bills-list · android · 14-upcoming-empty-paid-populated · light — \"Checked — nothing due. Paid bills are under Paid.\"\n15. f3-bills-list · ios · 15-loading · light — row skeleton.\n16. f3-bills-list · android · 16-error · light — InlineErrorRow with Retry.\n17. f3-bills-list · ios · 17-offline-stale · light — Maya's view, cached rows, stale line, overflow open with \"Mark paid\" disabled and \"Marking paid needs a connection.\"\n18. f3-bills-list · web-390 · 18-permission-denied · light — Jenna's guest view, no providers or amounts.\n19. f3-bills-list · ios · 19-worst-case · light — Sam's view, All segment with month overlines, longest provider, $3,412.56, 20+ rows; header \"4 upcoming · $3,718.73 through Mon 2 Nov · 1 overdue ($41.18)\".\n20. f3-bills-list · web-1440 · 20-member · light — Sam's view on desktop.\n21. f3-bills-list · ios · 21-ax5 · light — Sam's view at AX5, stacked rows.\n22. f3-bills-list · android · 22-200-percent · light — Sam's view at 200% font.\n23. f3-bills-list · ios · 23-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n24. f3-bills-list · ios · 01-upcoming-member-dense · dark — dark twin of 1.\n25. f3-bills-list · ios · 07-marked-paid-undo · dark — dark twin of 7.\n26. f3-bills-list · Notes — assumptions (the scope sentence switches to \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills\" after Jenna's guest access ends Tue 20 Oct; the Thu 17 Sep burst date was chosen so no bill was paid late and every bill in it was more than 3 days from due, so its notice stays quiet; Clark's September amount $109.60 matches the trend board; HOA dues are a calendar date, not a household bill, so they are outside this list and its totals even though the Foundations board draws an HOA BillRow specimen; the overdue amount is reported apart from the window total; rows keep the BillRow string \"Paid by Maya\" while bill detail uses the longer \"Marked paid by\" on purpose; the BillRow member variant is drawn as the header LockedActionRow plus \"Not marked paid yet\" in place of \"I paid this\" until the product decides; the race pattern \"Already marked paid by <name> · 6:02 PM\" is reserved for a future second person who can mark bills paid), every invented string (Theo, Jenna, NW Natural, State Farm, Waste Connections $38.75, the Thu 17 Sep payments, 6:02 PM, \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this screen.\"), the open decision on members recording \"I paid this\", and the note that the dashboard Bills card itself is drawn in f3-member-home-dashboard.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue. Turn 5: 25-26.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Removed the impossible 'Already marked paid by Sam' race variant from INTERACTION and COPY; kept the phone case and noted the '<name>' pattern on Notes (review major x2).",
              "Added dark twin 25 of frame 07; removed the 'omitted to stay in budget' note; Notes renumbered to 26; Turn 5 now 25-26 (review major).",
              "Moved the grouped burst from Tue 22 Sep to Thu 17 Sep on every row, frame 10, accessibility label and Notes, so no bill in it was within 3 days of due (review minor; matches f3-household-notifications).",
              "InlineUndo now reads 'Marked Clark Public Utilities paid · Undo' with 'We'll let Sam know when you leave this screen.' (page on web; omitted for Only-you bills); updated COPY and frame 7 (review minor).",
              "Header stated exactly: '3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov · 1 overdue ($41.18)', overdue kept out of the window total; worst case updated (review minor).",
              "Notes explain HOA dues are a calendar date, not a household bill, so they are outside the list and totals (review minor).",
              "Notes and LAYOUT state the BillRow member variant is drawn as the header LockedActionRow plus 'Not marked paid yet' in place of 'I paid this' until decided (review minor).",
              "Target sizes now '44pt iOS / 48dp Android / 44px web'; Notes record the deliberate 'Paid by' vs 'Marked paid by' difference (review minor).",
              "WHERE path reordered to 'Place tab › Larkspur Loop (place file) › Money section › Bills' (review minor).",
              "Denied copy no longer uses 'members' ('shared with Maya and Sam'); internal 'bill_paid' replaced with plain 'marked paid' notification wording; grouped arrival now names the 'See all 3 in Bills' line to match f3-household-notifications (consistency)."
