                    "issue": "On Android, the existing \"Share this address\" link sits inside the sticky wall, not near the aha card. The prompt says the wall stays \"unchanged\" and asks Claude Design to \"turn the existing single link into the pair\" 16dp below the card, but never says the link has to be moved out of the wall. ATTACH (2) also asks for a scroll position that shows the aha card and the link together, which is not possible because the link is pinned in the wall. Claude Design will either leave a share control in the wall, against the contract's WallBar rule, or draw it twice.",
                    "evidence": "PlaceLaunchScreen.kt:463-484: the bottom wall Column holds the wall text, PrimaryButton \"Continue\", the hold line, then `preview.place?.let { place -> ShareAddressLink(place) }`. The prompt says: \"Sticky wall, unchanged: \\\"Keep this address handy.\\\" and \\\"Continue\\\"\" and \"(2) Android address preview, same scroll, showing the existing \\\"Share this address\\\" link.\" component-contract.md TextActionRow doNot: \"No actions inside the sticky WallBar.\"",
                    "fix": "In TYPE, replace the Android sentence with: \"On Android, 'Share this address' currently sits in the sticky wall under 'Continue'. Remove it from the wall and redraw it as the first button of the pair, 16dp below the aha card. The wall keeps only its sentence, 'Continue' and the hold line.\" Change ATTACH (2) to: \"Android address preview showing the sticky wall with its current 'Share this address' link, plus a second screenshot scrolled to the aha card.\" In CONTENT, replace \"Sticky wall, unchanged\" with \"Sticky wall: as in the screenshot (iOS unchanged; Android minus the share link)\". Add a line to INSTEAD OF: \"Instead of leaving the Android share link in the wall, move it into the pair under the aha card — because the wall holds only the one primary.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The caption says \"never your address\" and sits directly under a button labelled \"Share this address\", which does send the address. A first-time reader could take the caption to cover both buttons and believe sharing the address hides it. That is a clarity and privacy-honesty failure right where the person decides to send.",
                    "evidence": "The prompt says: \"New row: \\\"Share this address\\\" · \\\"Compare with a friend\\\"\" and, under it, \"The card shows your city and your readings — never your address, and no name.\" It also says \"Share this address\\\" opens the system share sheet with the address link the Android app already sends\" (the URL is /start?address=<full address>).",
                    "fix": "Tie the caption to Compare. Change sentence 1 to \"The compare card shows your city and your readings — never your address, and no name.\" and log it on Notes as a surface delta to the Foundations caption, next to sentence 2. Also change the Share hint to \"Opens the share sheet. The link includes this address.\" Add to DONE WHEN: \"A reader can tell that 'Share this address' sends the address and 'Compare with a friend' does not.\""
