                    "issue": "The anatomy the prompt tells Claude Design to \"keep as they are\" exists only on web. The iOS and Android aha cards look different, and the prompt also says the attached screenshots are exact, so the two instructions contradict each other for frames 18 to 20 and 23. On native there is no overline, the tile is 34pt, the header chip is a tone-coloured grade chip whose text falls back to \"What stands out\", there is no source line, and the follow-up is a primary text link, not a sunken row. On iOS that link also goes straight to account creation instead of scrolling to the wall.",
                    "evidence": "PlacePreviewBody.swift ahaCard: `.frame(width: 34, height: 34)`, `PlaceChip(model: PlaceChipModel(tone: ahaChipTone(aha.tone), text: aha.grade.isEmpty ? \"What stands out\" : aha.grade))`, and the follow-up `Button(action: onCreateAccount)` in primary600. PlaceLaunchScreen.kt AhaCard has the same structure. Web AhaCard.tsx does have the overline, the 42px tile and the sunken follow-up. The prompt says: \"Keep these parts as they are: the overline \\\"WHAT STANDS OUT\\\" ..., the 42pt rounded icon tile, ... one sunken follow-up row with a chevron\" and \"The follow-up row scrolls to the sticky wall\".",
                    "fix": "In TYPE, say that the kept anatomy is the web card's. Add: \"On iOS and Android, change the card to the same anatomy: add the overline, move the chip to the right of the header row, enlarge the tile to 42pt, replace the tone-coloured grade chip with the neutral chip below, add the SourceCaption, and replace the primary text link with the sunken follow-up row. On native, the follow-up now scrolls to the wall instead of opening sign-up directly.\" Ask for native screenshots in ATTACH (2) marked \"layout changes as listed\", and add this conversion to Notes."
                  },
                  {
