                    "issue": "The follow-up copy promises something the product does not do automatically. Under the notification model, a saved place gets a reminder only when the person sets one and has granted notification permission. The default frame therefore makes a false promise at the moment of sign-up. The Notes flag the question, but the promise is still drawn as settled.",
                    "evidence": "The prompt says: \"Follow-up row: \\\"Keep this address to get a reminder before Mon 26 Oct\\\"\". ux-research-brief.md §3: \"Dates & bills ... On only for rows where the person set a reminder\". flows-spec flow-13 steps 3–4: the reminder is set later in x-date-sheet after the person picks a plan. The Notes say: \"confirm that a saved place gets a reminder for seeded civic dates\".",
                    "fix": "Change all three follow-up strings to \"Keep this address to set a reminder before Mon 26 Oct\" (and likewise for Tue 3 Nov and Mon 2 Nov), since the reader takes the action. Update the INSTEAD OF line and the Notes to match. Keep \"Keep this address handy\" as the fallback."
                  },
