                    "issue": "The calm-fallback headline states three facts from three authorities: no active alerts (weather service), air (AirNow) and floodplain (FEMA). Its caption names only AirNow, which breaks invariant 5 and the per-surface change, which requires naming what is calm \"with sources\". The FEMA status of the invented Seattle address is also an unlisted invented fact.",
                    "evidence": "The prompt says: \"Headline: \\\"No active alerts · Air Good today (AirNow) · Outside FEMA's mapped floodplain\\\"\" and \"Source: FILLED mark, \\\"Official\\\", then \\\"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\\\"\". per-surface-changes: \"Calm fallback names only what is actually calm, with sources\". The house-style invariant says: \"Sources are shown as a caption: authority · scope · as-of.\"",
                    "fix": "Give the calm card three stacked SourceCaptions, each with a filled mark: \"National Weather Service · alerts for this area · checked 6:10 PM\", \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\" and \"FEMA · area zone · effective <date>\". Print the word \"Official\" once. Add to Notes: \"4417 Densmore Ave N assumed outside FEMA's mapped floodplain and not radon Zone 1; check both.\""
                  },
