                    "issue": "The radon outbound string differs from the Foundations variant V2a, and the Notes do not log the difference. The prompt also claims Washington Dept of Health offers free kits, which no research finding confirms.",
                    "evidence": "00c-08 V2a reads \"Free test kits · Washington Dept of Health ↗\". The prompt reads \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\" and \"Never say 'free' unless the state offers free kits.\"",
                    "fix": "Keep the verb-led string. Add to Notes: \"Surface delta: outbound-test-kits reads 'Get a free test kit · …' (verb-led) instead of the Foundations 'Free test kits · …'. Confirm that WA DOH currently offers free kits before shipping the word 'free'.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The icon tile's glyph and colour are left undefined, so Claude Design will invent them. The existing tile uses tone tints, and the contract already defines KindGlyph tiles for voter registration and property tax.",
                    "evidence": "The prompt says: \"Keep ... the 42pt rounded icon tile\" but names no glyph. AhaCard.tsx uses `TILE[tone]`. The contract's KindGlyph: \"42pt rounded tile variant ... Set: ... property-tax (appeal / due), voter registration\".",
                    "fix": "Add to LAYOUT: \"Icon tile: the KindGlyph tile variant (voter registration or property-tax) in text.strong on surface.sunken for deadline cards; the existing hazard glyph in text.strong for radon, air and calm cards; no tone tint.\" Add KindGlyph to FOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The two prompts disagree about who sees the card, and one entry point is not an entry point. The share card only carries the headline. Frame 18 also shows only one button, while the native prompt specifies the pair.",
                    "evidence": "This prompt says \"Signed-out only.\" The native prompt says \"the row also shows for a signed-in account with no saved place\" on the same preview. The entry-point list includes \"The compare share card.\" Frame 18 says \"with \\\"Compare with a friend\\\" 16pt below the card.\"",
                    "fix": "Write: \"Signed out, or (native) signed in with no saved place.\" Drop \"The compare share card\" from the entry points; the headline still appears there. In frame 18, write \"with the TextActionRow share-compare pair 16pt below the card\"."
