                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "PLACE B is used as the 'no pickup rule and a quiet fortnight' fixture. That contradicts the shared fixture and the sibling prompts. PLACE B has a seeded Thursday pickup, and the statewide Mon 26 Oct voter deadline falls inside any 14-day window that starts Mon 19 Oct. So 'Checked — nothing in the next two weeks' would be a false all-clear.",
                    "evidence": "house-style-v2.txt: 'PLACE B ... Pickup weekday is Thursday per the City of Camas; frequency is Not set.' prompts f7-widget-tap-landing: 'Its strip shows hollow Thursday pickups on Thu 22 and Thu 29 Oct and the Mon 26 Oct voter bar.' f7-widget-gallery: 'Hollow pickup marks on Thu 22 and Thu 29 Oct.' Widget prompt: 'No pickup rule and a quiet fortnight (invented): PLACE B, label \"Birchfield Ct · Only you\"' and artboard 07 'PLACE B small and medium: \"Set your pickup day\" demoted, empty cells with the checked caption.' Invariant 4: the all-clear appears 'only when every check succeeded'.",
                    "fix": "Do not use PLACE B for this state. Invent a separate place (for example PLACE C), list it on Notes, and date the quiet-fortnight frame after Tue 3 Nov so that no statewide bar falls in the window. Or draw the no-rule state on its own, with the voter bar still present, and draw the nothing-due state on a different date. Keep PLACE B consistent with the other prompts: hollow Thursday pickups plus the Mon 26 Oct bar."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The voter deadline is worded as if it covered every method. The research brief requires method-specific wording, and Washington in-person registration stays open until 3 Nov. The strip item, the year lane and the large widget's spoken label all read 'voter registration must arrive by 26 Oct', which states a wrong closing date for in-person registration.",
                    "evidence": "ux-research-brief.md P18: 'word statutes exactly (\"must arrive by\"; per-method voter deadlines)'. Brief line 126: 'Wording is method-specific: \"Online or mail voter registration for Nov 3 must arrive by Oct 26 in Washington.\" ... Never state or imply registration status.' house-style: 'online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct; in person until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov.' Prompt: 'Mon 26 Oct voter registration must arrive by (Washington rule...)' and 'Next: voter registration must arrive by Monday 26 October.'",
                    "fix": "Use 'Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct' in the strip and lane descriptions and in the spoken label ('Next: online or mail voter registration must arrive by Monday 26 October'). If space forces a shorter visible form, list it on Notes and keep the method in the spoken label."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt says the confirm updates the widget only on 'the next snapshot'. The flow requires the confirm action itself, including the background tray action, to rewrite the snapshot at once. This is the exact gap the synthesis flagged.",
                    "evidence": "flows-spec.md flow row 8: 'The confirm action rewrites the snapshot at once, so the widget never keeps showing the hollow guess.' flows-spec line 76: 'The rule is confirmed in the background and the widget snapshot is rewritten without opening the app.' flows-spec line 486: 'No prompt says the widget snapshot (f7-today-widget) ... changes from hollow to tick on confirm'. Prompt: 'When someone confirms pickup, on Today or from the notification action, the next snapshot turns the hero's hollow ring into a tick.'",
                    "fix": "Reword: 'Confirming pickup, on Today or from the notification's \"That's my day\" action without opening the app, rewrites the snapshot immediately and reloads the widget, so the hollow ring becomes a tick with \"You · Tuesday\".' Add this rule to Notes."
                  },
