                    "evidence": "house-style-v2.txt invariant 2: 'Scope is always stated with one of two strings: \"Saved place · Only you\" or \"Your household\".' component-contract ScopeChip copyRules: 'Exactly these strings ... No other wording'. Prompt: 'Longest label: \"Birchfield Ct · Only you\"' and 'As space runs out, the hero wraps first, then the scope word drops, then the air row drops.'",
                    "fix": "Either use 'Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you' (and make that the longest-label test), or record 'Only you' as a deliberate widget short form on Notes, with the full string kept in the spoken label. Change the drop order so the air row goes before the scope word. The place label and the scope never drop."
