                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The ATTACH line asks for a screenshot of the current Nearby tab showing Invite rewards and Block Founders above the map. That screenshot cannot exist. Web has no referral UI today, and Block Founders still lives under Place › Your block. The house style also says attached hosts are exact, so the designer is told something false about the host.",
                    "evidence": "Prompt: \"ATTACH: ... the top of the Nearby tab, showing the Invite rewards card and Block Founders above the map\". inventory f9-invite-rewards-card hostSurface: \"Net-new on web (... web renders no referral UI at all)\". f9-block-founders-panel hostSurface: \"today it lives in Place > Your block\". house-style-v2: \"Attached host screenshots are exact\".",
                    "fix": "Attach only the current Nearby cells map. Say that the two cards above it are new and are drawn in prompts f9-invite-rewards-card and f9-block-founders-panel, and that their frames should be reused from those prompts, not from a screenshot."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The loading frame asks for a panel skeleton but never says to leave the SlotMeter row out of it. The contract forbids a skeleton for anything that fails closed, because an empty or placeholder meter reads as five open. The Block Founders prompt states this rule; this prompt does not.",
                    "evidence": "component-contract WarmingSkeleton doNot: \"No skeleton for anything that fails closed (the founding meter, the Earn row).\" SlotMeter doNot: \"No empty meter.\" Prompt: \"On a slow network, the map draws first and the panel shows a skeleton.\" and artboard 08 \"map drawn, panel skeleton\".",
                    "fix": "Add to EDGE CASES and artboard 08: \"The panel skeleton covers the title, homes, posts and last-post rows only. Draw no skeleton for the Founding slots row; it appears only after a successful lookup.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The list alternative is renamed. The Foundations component and the research change both call it 'List cells', but this prompt uses 'Show as a list', so the Foundations board and this screen will show different labels.",
                    "evidence": "component-contract PublicPointMap: \"Zoom +/- buttons and a 'List cells' alternative\". per-surface-changes: \"Add +/- and pan buttons and a 'List cells' view\". Prompt COPY: \"Show as a list\" · \"Show map\".",
                    "fix": "Use one string on both. Either keep 'List cells' or put the rename on Notes as a change to the Foundations variant."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The design reasoning behind the rectangles lost its anchor: the areas are geohash-6 cells, and that name was dropped. The stated size of 1.2 × 0.6 km, carried over from v1, is the size at the equator. At Vancouver's latitude (about 45.6°N), a geohash-6 cell is about 0.86 × 0.61 km, so the drawn 2:1 aspect is wrong.",
                    "evidence": "v1: \"Overlay geohash-6 cells, which are RECTANGLES roughly 1.2 km east–west by 0.6 km north–south\". Design doc F8: \"share a geohash-6\". Prompt: \"each about 1.2 km east–west by 0.6 km north–south\".",
                    "fix": "Write: \"areas are geohash-6 cells, about 0.86 km east–west by 0.61 km north–south at this latitude (roughly 1.4:1)\"."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The research requires the exclusion caption to be generated from the same fields that drive the behaviour, and to ship only once curator exclusion is live. This dependency is missing, so the caption could state an exclusion that isn't happening yet.",
                    "evidence": "research-findings (Why am I seeing this): \"Ship a line such as 'doesn't count as neighborhood activity' only once the de-curation code is live.\" Design doc F9 Seeder prompt: \"Exclude origin='curator' rows from the taper RPC and from every 'organic' count.\"",
                    "fix": "Add to Notes: \"'3 posts from Pantopus not counted' and 'Posts from Pantopus aren't counted.' depend on the F9 origin='curator' exclusion being live.\""
                  },
                  {
