                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt says to keep the existing unlock meters unchanged. In the shipped BlockDetail, those meters are 'N of M' progress bars with a fill (for example the bill benchmark at 4 of 10) and 'Unlocked' in success-coloured text. That breaks invariant 6 (no completion fractions) and P5, and the readable captions use text.muted. The same blanket 'keep everything unchanged' would also keep the existing 'Founding Neighbor · slot N of 5. Permanent.' line and the old 'permanent founding rank … keep their number forever' teaser.",
                    "evidence": "Prompt: \"Keep the existing unlock meters and every other existing element unchanged.\" BlockDetail.tsx:72 `{unlocked ? 'Unlocked' : `${current} of ${needed}`}` with a fill bar (:77). blockFoundersService.js:12 \"METERS per-section unlock progress (\\\"bill benchmark: 4 of 10\". house-style invariant 6: \"No ... completion fractions\". BlockDetail.tsx:162 \"Founding Neighbor · slot {founding.slot} of {founding.slots_total}. Permanent.\"",
                    "fix": "Either list the unlock meters as a change (state each one in words, for example 'Bill benchmark · needs 6 more verified homes', with no bar and no 'N of M') or remove them. State explicitly that the old tier line, the old teaser copy and any text.muted captions are replaced."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "Entry point (c) sends the 10-join referral reward 'Founding Neighbor badge' row to the dated first-5 tier block. That treats the referral badge and the Founding Neighbor tier as the same thing, which is the synonym the design doc's 'One name' item removes. It also contradicts the rewards prompt, where a locked row expands in place and does not navigate; Row C is locked for Maya.",
                    "evidence": "Prompt: \"The 'Founding Neighbor badge' row scrolls to the tier block.\" Design doc F9: \"'Block Founder #N' = rank; 'Founding Neighbor' = first-5 tier; referral tier renamed\" and \"rename tier 4 to 'Block Builder'\" (tier 4 = founding_badge at 10, inviteRewardService.js:23). Rewards prompt: \"A locked row expands in place with one sentence about the reward.\"",
                    "fix": "Delete the 'Founding Neighbor badge' entry. Entry (c) should be only 'Send a postcard invite' on Row A, which scrolls to the counter."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The window-closed degrade removes Maya's earned Founding Neighbor status. The fail-closed rule exists to withdraw a scarcity claim (open slots and the closing date). It was never meant to remove a badge someone already holds, and the shipped code shows the badge whenever is_founding is true, whatever the window state. Frame 06 shows 'rank and roster only' for Maya, who is one of the first 5.",
                    "evidence": "Prompt EDGE: \"Rank without tier: Maya after the window closes.\" Artboard 06: \"rank and roster only\". LAYOUT: \"when the window is closed ... drop the pill, the meter and the line\". BlockDetail.tsx:158-163 renders the Founding Neighbor line when founding.is_founding, independent of window_open. research: \"After it closes, the line disappears\" refers to the slots-open line.",
                    "fix": "For a holder, keep the 'Founding Neighbor' title and 'You're one of the first 5 homes verified on this block.' and drop only the SlotMeter and date pill. Show 'rank without tier' with a viewer who verified after the window (for example a #6)."
                  },
                  {
